lue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please do not rename my stuff - it is not yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Righty. Will change it back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T09:20:07-07:00","id":950080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=950075#post950075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. Righty. Will change it back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks - sorry if I was a bit snippy, it's just a bit of a sore spot for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T09:26:20-07:00","id":950086,"title":"","content":"Don't know if it's too powerful, but I was thinking something like this:<br /> <br /> Sphere incarnate(*** or *****)<br /> You can only purchase this at character creation.<br /> <br /> Choose one of your primary spheres. Your understanding of this Sphere is almost at an instinctual level.<br /> Benefit: whenever you spend a willpower point to gain a dice bonus on a non-magical skill roll, you can also spend 1 mana to increase the willpower bonus by a number equal to your sphere dots as long as this boost can somehow incorporate the chosen sphere.<br /> Example: Jo has life 2 and the 'life incarnate' merit. fighting for his life, Jo decides to put everything on this last punch. He spends a willpower to increase his next brawl roll. As he punches his opponent he feels his life magic surging forth (spends 1 mana) granting him extra strength. Instead of +3, he gets a total bonus of +5.<br /> Mary is a space incarnate with space 3. Running in the rooftops while being chased, she finds that she has to jump across a big gap. Fearing for her life, she spends a willpower point to help her with the athletics roll. As she jumps, she envisions the gap becoming smaller, as space tries to minimize the distance. For a willpower and a mana, she gains +6 instead of +3<br /> <br /> At 5 dots, this merit represents that you are one with the principles of your sphere, depending on your sphere you gain additional benefits:<br /> <br /> Space: you always know your surroundings, like a minimap. This effect has a radius equal to half your dots in space (round up). By spending a mana, multiply this radius by 10 for 1 turn.<br /> <br /> Life: you can spend a willpower point as an instant action. For rounds equal to half your life sphere dots (round up), you can spend a mana point to get the willpower bonus (including this merit's boost) on one physical, non magical, skill roll per round.<br /> <br /> Mind:by spending the willpower point as an instant action, you can increase the duration of this merit to half mind dots scenes, at the cost of 1 mana per scene. This boost can only be applied into non magical, mental, skill rolls.<br /> <br /> Prime: increase your dice pool to counterspell by half your prime dots<br /> <br /> Time: increase your initiative by half your time dots <br /> <br /> Matter:increase your non magical damage vs inanimate objects by half your matter dots<br /> <br /> Fate: you can reroll a single die in a non magical roll. You can do so half your fate dots times per chapter<br /> <br /> Spirit: this merit can be applied to ALL mundane skill rolls in umbra or while in twillight state. Spirits recognise you as an entity with half your spirit dots as your rank.<br /> <br /> Death: when you kill a living being of at least your size, gain a bonus equal to half your death dots on ALL rolls for the next turn.<br /> <br /> Forces: ???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T09:30:03-07:00","id":950090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=950080#post950080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks - sorry if I was a bit snippy, it's just a bit of a sore spot for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand. Hmm. Actually, you mind if I make my own version of the Merit instead? Personally, I can see the Mage Sight and Mage Armor being provided by two separate Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T09:37:24-07:00","id":950095,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11977\" data-vbnamecard=\"11977\">Shroudb</a> There aren't any spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T09:40:11-07:00","id":950096,"title":"","content":"Seeing as I like the concept of Arcana-Strewn Nature but feel the inclusion of two Attainments is too much, here's an alternative take on it. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Illumination</u> (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Proximi<br /> <b>Effect:</b> In addition to their Blessings, certain Proximi can peer into and gain insights from those threads of the Tapestry that they are resonant towards. By spending a point of Mana and Willpower each, they can use Active Mage Sight flavored according to a specific Blessing Arcanum. This Merit can be purchased up to three times, each keyed to a Blessing Arcanum. If a character possesses more than one version, he may spend additional Mana to invoke them during the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Illuminated Proximi suffer a more pronounced version of the drawback to using Active Mage Sight. They take a -4 modifier to all rolls unrelated to using or perceiving magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T09:41:43-07:00","id":950098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=950090#post950090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand. Hmm. Actually, you mind if I make my own version of the Merit instead? Personally, I can see the Mage Sight and Mage Armor being provided by two separate Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, go right ahead!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T09:56:41-07:00","id":950105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=950095#post950095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> There aren't any spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, sphere, arcana, potato potato","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11977-shroudb","name":"Shroudb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T22:17:34-07:00","id":950439,"title":"","content":"Here's something for those who favor the traditional method of crafting Perfected metals. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Seeker of Perfection</u> (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Awakened, Resolve or Composure 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The Mage has worked with Perfected metals by traditional means long enough that he can transmute them from their base substance with more efficiency. Each dot purchased in this Merit halves the minimum 'resting' period, rounded down, between every ten passes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:55:41-07:00","id":951259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=950063#post950063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a>. Added to a couple of your latest Merits here. <hr /><br /> <b><u>Paradox Eater</u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleeper or Fitful Slumber<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Some Sleepers and Sleepwalkers draw out the Abyss in a manner that allows them to draw strength from it. While the former achieves this through the shard of the Lie within their souls, the latter attain this power from the same exposure to magic that shocks them out of the Curse. Whenever a Paradox manifests in their presence, they may spend Willpower to roll a dice pool equal to their Integrity. Each success scored allows them to 'devour' one Reach and heal a point of lethal damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Taking Abyssal energy unto oneself can leave deep stains upon the soul. Each use of this Merit is treated as a Breaking Point. Furthermore, whenever a Mage must roll for Paradox in the character's presence, he adds an additional die to the Paradox pool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Herald</u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Certain Sleepwalkers can not only bear a Mage's spells, but maintain them through force of will should they be conferred into their hands. An Awakened character may spend a Willpower point to anchor a spell into a willing Sleepwalker's soul. The Sleepwalker can maintain a number of active spells equal to the higher of Resolve or Composure. Any spell in excess of this limit is treated as if it were relinquished with a Willpower point.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Paradox Eater (and its kin), what about the ability to acquire and act as a &quot;carrier&quot; for Paradox Conditions? Sleepers can't really be affected by most of them, but maybe they automatically pass them off to Mages they near/touch/witness-the-spell-casting-of?<br /> <br /> Hmm. The point of Herald was to give a Sleepwalker more control over the spells they hold. But I just reread the section and Mages don't actually have much more control over spells already cast. So not much usefulness. Maybe allow said Sleepwalkers to be Imbued, as per Imbue item, granting them a few spells they can &quot;cast&quot; by releasing them?<br /> <hr /><br /> Hmm. What about a Sleepwalker Merit that let's them borrow a Mage's Occultation via the magic/Spell they are Holding? One the one hand, this renders them harder to detect, ideally even by the Mage's enemies. On the other, it drives them away from everyone else (who start to forget them). I could see it especially common among pawns/cultists of the Mad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-15-2016, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T22:08:51-07:00","id":951502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=951259#post951259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Paradox Eater (and its kin), what about the ability to acquire and act as a &amp;quot;carrier&amp;quot; for Paradox Conditions? Sleepers can't really be affected by most of them, but maybe they automatically pass them off to Mages they near/touch/witness-the-spell-casting-of?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea. Not sure if it skirts too close to that one Sleepwalker Merit that deals in Paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=951259#post951259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. The point of Herald was to give a Sleepwalker more control over the spells they hold. But I just reread the section and Mages don't actually have much more control over spells already cast. So not much usefulness. Maybe allow said Sleepwalkers to be Imbued, as per Imbue item, granting them a few spells they can &amp;quot;cast&amp;quot; by releasing them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do try writing this down please x3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=951259#post951259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. What about a Sleepwalker Merit that let's them borrow a Mage's Occultation via the magic/Spell they are Holding? One the one hand, this renders them harder to detect, ideally even by the Mage's enemies. On the other, it drives them away from everyone else (who start to forget them). I could see it especially common among pawns/cultists of the Mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. This could work. Try elaborating on it some more with a writeup if possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:00:49-07:00","id":952178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=951502#post951502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting idea. Not sure if it skirts too close to that one Sleepwalker Merit that deals in Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which one is that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=951502#post951502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do try writing this down please x3</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Herald (\u2022+, Special)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The character can now act as if they were an object for the purposes of Imbued Item. Spells (and Mana) can be placed in their care so that they can then later active them. Treat this as Imbued Item (regarding dot totals and their effects), except it is the character holding the magic, not an item in their possession, and they may spend Willpower in place of Mana to activate the spell.<br /> <b>Note:</b> Each spell held takes up one instance of Spell Control that the Sleepwalker can hold. The Banner Carrier merit is recommended for the capacity of holding more than a few spells. Alternatively, the Mage who cast the Imbued spell can Release it, with all the consequences that implies.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Turning people into Imbued Items since 2016. Though while writing, it occurs to me you might be able to accomplish similar results with Imbued tattoos <i>and</i> get some sweet tattoo magic in there.]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=951502#post951502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. This could work. Try elaborating on it some more with a writeup if possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Second-hand Secrecy (\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You can borrow some of the obscuring nature of Supernal Magic and your patron Mage's Occultation. When holding a Spell for a Mage, you can also take advantage of their level of Occultation (as per the Merit) as if you possessed it.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> This effect also extends to Sleepers as if the character were one of the Mad. They quickly become forgotten by the normal world at large, and this separation can drive many Sleepwalkers insane or into unhealthy dependency with Awakened masters.<br /> [<u>Comment</u>: Yes, your Sleepwalker Banner Carriers are safer from detection, but they also are cut off from their peers and family. This also makes Mad One cults a shadowy nightmare that fade from awareness and are difficult to track just as much as their leader.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-07-2016, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T23:51:25-07:00","id":952359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=952178#post952178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which one is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't recall atm. But I know it allowed a Sleepwalker to willingly suffer a Paradox Condition from a Mage to humble them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=952178#post952178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Herald (\u2022+, Special)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The character can now act as if they were an object for the purposes of Imbued Item. Spells (and Mana) can be placed in their care so that they can then later active them. Treat this as Imbued Item (regarding dot totals and their effects), except it is the character holding the magic, not an item in their possession, and they may spend Willpower in place of Mana to activate the spell.<br /> <b>Note:</b> Each spell held takes up one instance of Spell Control that the Sleepwalker can hold. The Banner Carrier merit is recommended for the capacity of holding more than a few spells.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Turning people into Imbued Items since 2016. Though while writing, it occurs to me you might be able to accomplish similar results with Imbued tattoos <i>and</i> get some sweat tattoo magic in there.]</div> </div> </div> </div>This looks much better. I'll take a look at a similar Merit done by PenDragon and make a comparison between the two before I give more constructive critique.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=952178#post952178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Second-hand Secrecy (\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You can borrow some of the obscuring nature of Supernal Magic and your patron Mage's Occultation. When holding a Spell for a Mage, you can also take advantage of their level of Occultation (as per the Merit) as if you possessed it.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> This effect also extends to Sleepers as if the character were one of the Mad. They quickly become forgotten by the normal world at large, and this separation can drive many Sleepwalkers insane or into unhealthy dependency with Awakened masters.<br /> [<u>Comment</u>: Yes, you Sleepwalker Banner Carriers are safer from detection, but they also are cut off from their peers and family. This also makes Mad One cults a shadowy nightmare that fade from awareness and are difficult to track just as much as their leader.]</div> </div> </div> </div>Dang. Now,<i> that</i> is harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:14:39-07:00","id":952492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=952359#post952359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't recall atm. But I know it allowed a Sleepwalker to willingly suffer a Paradox Condition from a Mage to humble them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ritual Martyr? That only applies to a Sleepwalker participating in Rituals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=952359#post952359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This looks much better. I'll take a look at a similar Merit done by PenDragon and make a comparison between the two before I give more constructive critique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? I'd be interested in the comparison as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=952359#post952359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dang. Now,<i> that</i> is harsh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you don't <i>have</i> to hold spells or borrow Occultation. Just be aware the extra &quot;cover&quot; comes with costs.<br /> <br /> And beware Mad Cults where this is common. They could have a slew of Spell carrying cultists hiding out in a tenement <i>and no one would know</i>. Just make sure they get food and water occasionally.<br /> <hr /><br /> What about one that lets a Sleepwalker perform an Oblation for Mana? Only at Hallows? Once per day/week?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:04:49-07:00","id":953939,"title":"","content":"Some more, this time for Mage-Hunters <hr /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Spell Thief (Supernatural, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Sleepwalker</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> You can touch the subject of a spell, spend 1 Willpower point, and make a Clash of Wills roll using Willpower to take control of that spell. If successful, the spell is now treated as if you were the Mage who cast it (Rolling any additional Clash of Wills regarding it using your Willpower). When you steal the spell, you may at that moment alter the target to yourself (you are unable to do so in the future). After that, you may maintain the spell, cancel it, or even Release it. You can only steal control of spells whose highest Arcana is equal to or less than your dots in this merit.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> You can only maintain a number of spells via this method equal to the lower of your Resolve or Composure - additional spells are automatically cancelled unless you choose to Release them. Additionally, you are marked by the Nimbus of each Mage who's spell you\u2019ve stolen.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Swipe the defensive spells from a Mage? Sure. Take the life extension magics from a Mage for yourself? No problem. &quot;Eat&quot; the hex from a buddy and then cancel it? Go right ahead. You could even assemble a rickety collection of enchantments by Releasing them. Warranty gets void, though.]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Spell Mimic (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Spell Thief \u2022+, Herald \u2022+</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> You can now copy and retain spells that you\u2019ve usurped. Whenever you take control of a spell with Spell Thief, you can later treat it as if a Mage Imbued it into you as per Herald.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Whenever you integrate a spell into your Pattern, you are immediately affected by the Immediate Nimbus of the Mage who cast it.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Don't just swipe existing magics - copy them for later use. Some side effects may occur.]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Spell Catch (\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Spell Thief \u2022+</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> You can now engage in a spell Dodge action against aimed spells - whenever you succeed in your Dodge roll against the aimed spell, you may attempt to take control of it as if you used Spell Thief. The following turn, you may \u201credirect\u201d it at another target, or cancel it.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: When the lightning bolts fly, you can amaze your friends and confound your foes by throwing them back like a hot potato. Just remember you have no such defense against more indirect assaults.]<br /> <br /> Oh, I also added an addendum to the Drawback for Herald - you can get around it by having whoever cast the Imbued Spell Release it, with the usual consequences depending on the method (discount Deviants who've had &quot;their&quot; spell's sloppily Released? Sure!).</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-19-2016, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:20:28-07:00","id":956614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=952492#post952492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? I'd be interested in the comparison as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take was closer to a subsplat than a merit, but is conceptually similar. I buffed the Imbued subject slightly so they can better use the spell's they are given, and made a couple entries for how one might become imbued (Mages aren't the only option). Give it a look: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#heading=h.e6p06i9c4368\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...h.e6p06i9c4368</a><br /> <br /> P.S. I quite like the second hand secrecy merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T06:44:54-07:00","id":957570,"title":"","content":"So, wrestling with an idea for a merit that allows you to use your emotions to fuel your magic. Magic requires Will, but emotions can fuel that at a cost of precision. Something like you can take one or two dice using emotions as a Yantra, but for each die you take the ST gets a free Reach to assign how they want similar to what they get when there's a Paradox. Also these Reach stack with any Paradox Reach if it comes up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:58:30-07:00","id":957752,"title":"","content":"Do a standard +1 for feeling a strong emotion and +2 for feeling emotion so strong that it bestows a Condition upon you, with maybe +3 being what you described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:31:38-07:00","id":957774,"title":"","content":"I was thinking more along the lines of being able to do the +1 for free, taking an appropriate emotional Condition (Shaken, Spooked, Swooning, etc) to access the +2. The player gets extra dice and the ST gets some Reach to mess around with the Magic a bit. I've got a player who is shooting for a kind of Dresden feeling for his character and more oomph less precision would fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:33:50-07:00","id":957776,"title":"","content":"You could also just roll it into Shadow Name; Mage whose identity is prone to emotional outburst could reign them in for persona yantra. <br /> Though in general a +1 for &quot;something with no cost&quot;, +2 for &quot;condition or resource&quot; and +3 &quot;rare resource or condition+resource&quot; seems like a good rule of thumb for yantras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:39:15-07:00","id":957778,"title":"","content":"I don't know, maybe it's just me, but doesn't that seem like what spending Willpower is supposed to represent? I mean, unless the Merit locks in a specific kind of emotion.<br /> <br /> On that note, maybe you could play around with the bonuses by having a Drawback of &quot;When not feeling/under the influence of the emotion, spell casting rolls suffer a -X penalty&quot;, with X being the inverse of the bonus? Representing that the caster has become <i>dependent</i> upon using their emotional state as a Yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:24:50-07:00","id":957842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=957776#post957776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also just roll it into Shadow Name; Mage whose identity is prone to emotional outburst could reign them in for persona yantra. <br /> Though in general a +1 for &quot;something with no cost&quot;, +2 for &quot;condition or resource&quot; and +3 &quot;rare resource or condition+resource&quot; seems like a good rule of thumb for yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't want to venture into +3 territory. I don't think this qualifies, everyone has emotions and this isn't that exclusive an ability. This would just represent a slightly rarefied use of them for magical means.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> I kind of figured that the ST getting to mess around with the spell via &quot;special&quot; Reach was probably already drawback enough. That said, yes WP is pretty good for that kind of thing, but it isn't any more sloppy than not using it which is what I'm shooting for. This is kind of a middle step between a Mage's usual precision and the sloppiness of risking Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-25-2016, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T14:33:13-07:00","id":957846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=957842#post957842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I don't want to venture into +3 territory. I don't think this qualifies, everyone has emotions and this isn't that exclusive an ability. This would just represent a slightly rarefied use of them for magical means.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> I kind of figured that the ST getting to mess around with the spell via &quot;special&quot; Reach was probably already drawback enough. That said, yes WP is pretty good for that kind of thing, but it isn't any more sloppy than not using it which is what I'm shooting for. This is kind of a middle step between a Mage's usual precision and the sloppiness of risking Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about allowing Willpower Risk, like from Hunter 1E? Succeed, and you get to keep the Willpower, but failure becomes Dramatic Failure.<br /> <br /> &lt;shrug&gt; I could easily see &quot;I was really angry and channeled more power than was prudent&quot; as the narrative to mechanically using more Reach. Using Reach (over your free allotment) already carries connotations of power for risk, and being angry or afraid is certainly IC reason enough to go for that gamble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T16:46:27-07:00","id":957923,"title":"","content":"Yes, it could, but it's not an unknown gamble or risk in the same way as what I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T20:33:02-07:00","id":958029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=957923#post957923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it could, but it's not an unknown gamble or risk in the same way as what I want.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. I wish there were a consolidated Emotions system, like Beast's max feeding threshold (Changeling could use it for harvesting Glamour). That would make the exact numeric effects easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T09:51:10-07:00","id":958271,"title":"","content":"Another Abyssal+Sleeper Merit idea: Something something influence of the Abyss allows the character to do something &quot;impossible&quot;, like the Skill Tricks in Mirrors... but for the wrong skills. Like using Empathy on Computers, or Intimidate in place of Firearms. Or something. You know, leverage the &quot;the Abyss is a source of impossibilities&quot; and the &quot;Sleepers have a Shard of the Abyss&quot; to make a person into a really minor Abyssal Intrusion in a way that <i>seems</i> magical, but would horrify any (non-Scelesti) Mage who took a closer look.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T12:57:20-07:00","id":965813,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Passionate Sorcery (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mage<br /> <b>Effects:</b> You can draw upon your emotions to fuel your magic. You gain a +1 Yantra bonus as long as you are under the effects of an appropriate <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/300316-intense-emotional-states-and-you-system?p=302238#post302238\">Strong [Emotion]</a> Condition - this increases to a +2 if you are currently under the effects of Obsessive [Emotion] for the same emotion. If casting a spell would let you take a Beat from either Condition, you may take an Arcane Beat instead.<br /> <b>Drawbacks:</b> Letting your emotions rule you this way is... unwise. If a spell benefiting from the Yantra bonus granted by this Merit would be a Wisdom Sin, you take a penalty on the roll to prevent degeneration equal to the Yantra bonus.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Awakened Feng Shui (Style; \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Hallow \u2022+<br /> <b>Lay the Arrangement (\u2022):</b> You may spend a day carefully aligning and arranging your Hallow, giving it an Open Condition themed after the Resonance of one of the contributing Ley-Lines. As long as this Open Condition remains, that Hallow can hold additional Tass equal to twice your dots in Awakened Feng Shui. If the Open Condition is removed, any Tass past the normal limit immediately spoils.<br /> <b>Resonant Harvest (\u2022\u2022):</b> As long as the Open Condition remains on your Hallow, any Tass you take from it is <i>concentrated</i>. Whenever you spend the Tass, any Persona Yantra you get from it increases to +2.<br /> <b>Resonant Redoubt (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> As long as the Hallow has the Open Condition, you may reduce the amount of Tass the Hallow can store by 3 to increase your Gnosis by 1 for the purposes of Spell Control - you may do so a number of times equal to your dots in Awakened Feng Shui. These additional Spell Control slots can only be used to hold spells that match the Hallow's Resonance.<br /> <i>Drawback</i>: If the Open condition is removed from your Hallow, any spells supported by the Hallow are immediately relinquished as if you had spent a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Supernal Truespeech (Style; \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> High Speech, Prime \u2022+<br /> <b>The World Listens (\u2022):</b> As long as you are speaking in the glossolalia of High Speech, you cannot be silenced - you could clearly and audibly enunciate the words in a gale-force wind or vacuum, and can intelligibly speak with a slit throat or crushed voice-box. You also gain a bonus on any Social roll made while speaking High Speech equal to half your dots in this merit, rounded up.<br /> <b>Speaking the Higher Name (\u2022\u2022):</b> You may combine the Mantra Yantra with the use of someone's Sympathetic Name as a Yantra with devastating results. While doing so still counts as using two Yantras, you may add your Yantra bonus from High Speech directly to the spell's Primary Factor instead of adding it to your dice pool.<br /> <b>Supernal Filibuster (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> You may combine the Mantra Yantra with the Concentration Yantra, babbling platonic truths while you maintain your spells. As long as you continue to speak while concentrating on the spell, ignore any Paradox the spell caused - it is delayed until you finish speaking, at which point it applies immediately.<br /> <i>Drawback</i>: Delaying the Abyss in this manner is dangerous - increase the Paradox dice pool as if you had Reached past your safe limit.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Nightmares (\u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Banisher, Wits \u2022\u2022\u2022, Composure \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Benefits:</b> Unlike most Mages, your dreams are a surreal nightmare realm of pure, unrelenting terror. You may enter your own dreams without a meditation roll whenever you fall asleep. In addition, your dots in the Nightmares merit count as dots in the Safe Place merit for the purposes of your dreams - use Occult instead of Crafts when determining whether or not you can leave traps, which can be bypassed with a Finesse + Mind roll, penalized by your dots in Nightmares.<br /> <b>Drawbacks:</b> You cannot avoid any damage caused by any traps you leave in your own dreams. What's worse, you suffer a level of Lethal damage whenever you enter your own dreams, and do not regain any Willpower on nights where you do so.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ideosyncratic Arcana (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 3+<br /> <b>Benefits:</b> You have stumbled upon a fragment of Supernal knowledge unknown to the majority of the Wise. Upon taking this merit, define a new Arcana - pick a &quot;truth&quot; and a number of words equal to twice your dots in this merit to form that Arcana's purview, and work with your ST to determine the precise effects it has with regards to Mage Sight and its Attainments. If you took the two-dot version of this Merit, treat the Ideosyncratic Arcana as if it were an Inferior Arcana - for four dots, you can treat it as a Common Arcana.<br /> <b>Drawbacks:</b> This bizarre partial-arcana is fragile and feral - each dot you learn is a Sin against Falling Wisdom, and spells that belong to the Arcana treat any Dissonance roll that scores three or more Successes as an Exceptional Success.<br /> <b>Special:</b> If you do not already have a Legacy and have 4 dots in this merit, you may found a Legacy that uses your Ideosyncratic Arcana as its third Ruling Arcana.<br /> <br /> <i>(Yeah, this merit is for pretty &quot;special&quot; games. You </i>really<i> want to ask your ST permission before taking this one.)</i><br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Wise Sleepwalker (\u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Proximi<br /> <b>Effects:</b> Your mindset is closer to a Mage's than you'd think - you lose the Integrity advantage. Instead, you gain Wisdom at a rating equal to your previous Integrity score, as well as a single Obsession. You may spend Arcane Experience to purchase Blessings.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit of the Edit:</b> I rebalanced Supernal Truespeech a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 09-09-2016, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T11:42:33-07:00","id":966352,"title":"","content":"Can anyone access GDocs from the first post? I can open only the first one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/120-daimon","name":"Daimon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T13:43:47-07:00","id":966414,"title":"","content":"Nope - Deionscribe needs to change the permissions for the other ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T13:46:04-07:00","id":966416,"title":"","content":"Great job on the Merits, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a>. Do you think spelling out the inherent benefits of Wisdom (being able contain Paradoxes, etc.) is worth mentioning, or no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T15:29:41-07:00","id":966463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=966416#post966416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great job on the Merits, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a>. Do you think spelling out the inherent benefits of Wisdom (being able contain Paradoxes, etc.) is worth mentioning, or no?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope - I try to avoid bloating when I write stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:37:22-07:00","id":966633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daimon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=966352#post966352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone access GDocs from the first post? I can open only the first one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll fix the settings for the GDocs when I log in later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T08:53:44-07:00","id":966777,"title":"","content":"Fixing a typo:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Harsh Insight (\u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> A dot in that particular Arcana<br /> <b>Effects:</b> You have a peculiarly <i>strong</i> view of one of your Ruling Arcana, manifesting itself with violence upon your perspectives. You are <i>always</i> considered to be under the effects of active Mage sight incorporating that Arcana - this does not allow you to use focused Mage Sight and does not carry the normal penalty unless you actually enter active Mage Sight. In addition, you may spend one Mana when casting a Knowing or Unveiling spell belonging to that Arcana to use your dots in Harsh Insight in place of that spell's base Potency.<br /> <b>Drawbacks:</b> This sort of insight into the Arcana brings with it troubling dreams and a separation from the Fallen World - you may treat dots in Harsh Insight as dots in Seer of the Throne Status for the purposes of taking the Prelacy merit. You also suffer a penalty to all Social rolls equal to half your dots in Harsh Insight, rounded up - subtract your dots in the Prelacy merit from your dots in this merit when determining this penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T09:09:58-07:00","id":966781,"title":"","content":"Okay, everyone. All the Google Docs should be accessible, now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T01:42:20-07:00","id":970571,"title":"","content":"Came up with this to make Runes a little more usable for my current character. It seems like it'd mesh well with the other Rune merits in this doc, so feel free to include it. Not 100% sure on the balance for it, so please let me know what you think.<br /> <br /> The idea is that her and her cabal will all have various runes tattooed onto them.<br /> In this context 'The spell being used' = The name of the spell, eg 'Telepathy', 'Mend', 'Decay', etc<br /> <br /> <b>Disjointed Runes</b><b> (\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Awakened<br /> <b>Effect: </b>You possess an innate understanding of how each component symbol of a given rune functions on its own.<br /> With the three dot version of this merit, you may inscribe runes that describe aspects of a spell. You can combine these into a single Imago, instead of inscribing a set of runes that describes only a single Imago.<br /> <br /> In order to use the Runes Yantra, all aspects of the spell must be described on the subjects of the spell. Aspects include:<br /> Any Reach effects applied to the spell<br /> Any Spell Factors<br /> The Spell being used.<br /> <br /> If the mage has existing runes describing these aspects, they may cast the spell without inscribing new runes.<br /> <br /> With the five dot version of this merit, the Runes Yantra gives a +1 bonus for each aspect that your runes describe, instead of a flat +2 . You may use the Runes Yantra without describing all aspects.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:48:58-07:00","id":973846,"title":"","content":"Based on a misconception of how the Artifact Arcana worked, I bring you this merit, that lets them work the way I thought they worked (more or less). I'm restricting it to Sleepwalkers to make it interesting - you could probably run a game/Chronicle of PCs with this, and influence what Arcana they have access to and when by controlling what Artifacts they have access to at the time. <hr /><br /> <b>Relic Adept (\u2022\u2022+)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker, Relic Attuned<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You can invoke more complex spells than an Artifact possesses, using a combination of your arcane knowledge and the Artifact's Supernal power. Pick one Practice - when holding an Artifact, you can cast spells using that Practice as if you were a Mage with the Artifact's Gnosis and Arcana. You must still pay for the Mana costs with the Artifact's Mana, any you might possess (such as through Cup Bearer), or Willpower (such as through Relic Attuned), and you still lack Wisdom to contain Paradoxes with. You have Spell Control equal to a Mage with the same Gnosis as the Artifact. Spells are automatically ended at the end of any scene where you no longer retain ownership over the Artifact (unless you Relinquish it).<br /> <br /> For each additional dot, you can learn a new Practice of that level. For instance, learning Compelling would add one dot, while learning Fraying would add three dots.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-04-2016, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:49:08-07:00","id":997894,"title":"","content":"<b>Conductive (\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022, or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Through some quirk of Destiny, biology, or magic, you conduct Supernal energies far easier than the rest of the Fallen World. Whenever a spell is cast on you, its Potency is treated as if it were 1, 2, or 3 higher (respectively for the one, three, and five dot versions of the merit), solely as it applies to you (the Potency is its original value against all other targets it might effect).<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The Potency is increased for all spells - including non-beneficial ones.<br /> <br /> And the inverse, though I'm worried about this being too strong<br /> <br /> <b>Grounded (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Non-Awakened<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Something in your nature impedes the flow of Supernal Truth, reducing the Potency of any magic that affects you by half of the dots in this merit. Since this is reduced Potency, and not merely an increased Withstand rating, it even affects spells that aren't Withstood (such as Fraying spells).<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The reduced Potency cannot be lowered and affects even beneficial magic.<br /> <br /> Just for fun, some potential Advanced versions of the above. Result may vary wildly, and access is something a ST should consider thoroughly beforehand.<br /> <br /> <b>Conductive, Advanced (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Conductive \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Supernal energies flow through you quickly and readily. Any spell that targets you has an extra free Reach, albeit it is only effective as it pertains to you. This could mean increased Potency, including you &quot;for free&quot; by applying it to Scale, or an additional Reach effect.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The free Reach is available to less benign spells cast at you as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Grounded, Advanced (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Grounded \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Supernal energies avoid you and disappear into the void of your attachment to the Lie. Any spell targeting you must spend an additional point of Reach, solely to affect you.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The increase Reach cost applies to <i>all</i> magic that targets you - even spells you'd welcome or that could save your life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-07-2016, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T23:28:58-07:00","id":998110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=997894#post997894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would a merit look for something like this?<br /> <br /> [Name] [\u25cfs]<br /> Prerequisites: Sleepwalker<br /> Effect: Through some quirk of Destiny, biology, or magic, you conduct Supernal energies far easier than the rest of the Fallen World. Whenever a spell is cast on you, its Potency is treat as if it were [1] higher, solely as it applies to you (the Potency is its original value against all other targets it might effect).<br /> Drawback: The Potency is increased for all spells - including non-beneficial ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would put it at 1, 3, and 5 dots, with the Merit raising Potency on the subject by half its rating. As for a name, how does Conduit sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T07:06:44-07:00","id":998210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=998110#post998110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would put it at 1, 3, and 5 dots, with the Merit raising Potency on the subject by half its rating. As for a name, how does Conduit sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I went with Conductive to fit its mirror Grounded in terminology. I updated the original, and added the inverse and Advanced versions of both. Tell me what you think?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T08:56:40-07:00","id":998786,"title":"","content":"So, I've been thinking about cryptopolies lately, because I am always thinking about cryptopolies. While this isn't really much of a homebrew merit, it is something I'd appreciate feedback on and can't think of anywhere more appropriate to post it.<br /> <br /> Building on the structure of 1e's information in the Ladder book, a cryptopoly is a collection of interwoven cults and conspiracies at the top of which sit Illuminates - thearchs and their trusted Sleepwalkers - who are directed in their activities by the local deacon. Outside of their official capacities for the deacon, though, a cryptopoly cult's resources are open to those of other thearchs to use as needed.<br /> <br /> To represent the cryptopoly system, two merits are necessary: Mystery Cult Influence and Allies/Contacts (Cryptopoly).<br /> <br /> Mystery Cult Influence is in the Mage core. In a cryptopoly, the three dot level is available for every thearch member of the Caucus, representing the basic advantages of being a prince of the heavens. Four dots are usually reserved for Illuminates, who have more direct control over a cult. Five dots is reserved for deacons. Exceptions exist but this is the general structure.<br /> <br /> While there are no hard-and-fast rules in designing the benefits of a cult, the &quot;standard&quot; cryptopoly spread for three dots are two dots of Allies (Cryptopoly), one dot of Contacts (Cryptopoly), and one dot of Resources. This can (and probably should) be tweaked depending on the cryptopoly's local structure. One that has deep connections focused on law enforcement, say, may not be as financially powerful but its members are always able to find friends in the local police (switching Resources for Allies (Law Enforcement)).<br /> <br /> And that brings me to the actual modestly homebrew part of this:<br /> <br /> <b>Allies/Contacts (Cryptopoly)</b><br /> <br /> You are a thearch; part of the ruling class of the Awakened Nation. For that reason, you have been given unparalleled access to a subversive network that has infiltrated the structure of the region to a degree that many might be truly astonished by. Wherever you have need, you will find a friend indeed.<br /> <br /> This merit functions similarly to those of the same type, except that it may theoretically apply in just about any situation. The reach of the Silver Ladder is longer than many suspect. Even if the Mage personally has no direct means of making connections, all it takes is a phone call or a letter couriered to the right person and the doors to the halls of power will open. In short, in any situation where the Mage might use the Allies or Contacts merits, this merit may apply (with ST approval; the Ladder's reach is long, but not universal).<br /> <br /> In addition, the cryptopoly merit may be allowed (again, with ST approval) to stack with other Allies dots that the player already possesses; triggering additional agents within the organization to make a given task less onerous or risky on their contacts. Thus, a Mage with Allies 2 (Police) and Allies 2 (Cryptopoly) may use both at once to treat themselves as having four Allies dots for a given favour. Doing so counts as a use for both merits, however, and pings the Drawback of this one as it would if used alone.<br /> <br /> <i>Drawback:</i> There is a downside, of course, to the connections you tug upon not being personal. Everyone can find out what you've been doing, just by asking. While Illuminates are rarely profligate with their secrets, they know what you've been up to and that means they can tell anyone. Thus, unwise is the thearch who abuses these benefits too readily. While thearchs tend to be lax on certain definitions of &quot;abuse of power&quot; - no-one looks askew at the thearch who uses the cryptopoly to pursue their Obsessions or even just for basic ambitions, like getting city council to speedily approve your business plans - using it repeatedly to get out of trouble with the law or in ways that are harmful to Sleepers will draw the eyes of their fellows.<br /> <br /> If a character uses personal Allies combined with cryptopoly ones, an Investigation roll is needed to find out what they were up to, with a penalty (or bonus) equal to the difference in the number of personal vs. cryptopoly dots used (that is, if the character used three personal dots and two cryptopoly dots, the subsequent Investigation roll would take a -1 penalty).<br /> <br /> (Note: For adjudicating the above, expect that any thearch can learn about the cryptopoly uses of any thearch of equal or lesser standing in the Mystery Cult Influence background.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T19:18:53-08:00","id":1014098,"title":"","content":"Working on a Spellbreaker Style Merit that uses Countermagic Stance as one of its prerequisites. It's going to be three dots at least, with the first two benefits being as described.<br /> <br /> o -- When you employ the Counterspell Attainment, you may identify the Practice and Spell Factors of the the target spell.<br /> <br /> oo -- You may spend a Willpower point to cast a successfully countered spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-07-2016, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T09:15:50-08:00","id":1014336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1014098#post1014098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Working on a Spellbreaker Style Merit that uses Countermagic Stance as one of its prerequisites. It's going to be three dots at least, with the first two benefits being as described.<br /> <br /> o -- When you employ the Counterspell Attainment, you may identify the Practice and Spell Factors of the the target spell.<br /> <br /> oo -- You may spend a Willpower point to cast a successfully countered spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any limitations or stipulations on that copy?<br /> <br /> Hmm. Taking a concept from M:tG, might you be able to impose a Condition that blocks or interferes with spells you counter? So not only can you shut down <i>that</i> spell, but you can prevent/inhibit them from casting that spell again (which is situational, but definitely handy if you can lock out their attack spell Praxis).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T09:43:41-08:00","id":1014345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1014336#post1014336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any limitations or stipulations on that copy?<br /> <br /> Hmm. Taking a concept from M:tG, might you be able to impose a Condition that blocks or interferes with spells you counter? So not only can you shut down <i>that</i> spell, but you can prevent/inhibit them from casting that spell again (which is situational, but definitely handy if you can lock out their attack spell Praxis).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see what you're suggesting work as the second-dot benefit so I can bump up the ability to redirect a countered spell with a Willpower expenditure to the third dot. How long would it last, though? For a scene? Or would it last a number of turns equal to the countering Mage's dots in the relevant Arcanum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T10:19:23-08:00","id":1014357,"title":"","content":"Inspired by the aimed spell thread....<br /> <br /> <b>Magister Virgae (Style, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Awakened<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your character is particularly adept with the use of a particular magic tool. So long as she is casting spells using this tool as a Dedicated Magical Tool she benefits from the effects of this Merit. The tool must be something wielded by hand.<br /> <b>Conduit (</b><b>\u2022): </b>When casting an aimed spell, the mage receives a +1 bonus to the die roll to aim the spell.<br /> <b>Mnemonic (</b><b>\u2022\u2022): </b>The mage traces Atlantean runes in the air with her tool as she casts a spell. Her tool now gives an additional +1 bonus to the spellcasting pool when used as a Yantra.<br /> <b>Corpus (</b><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>The tool's durability increases by 1 and the mage's sympathy with it increases to Connected. She is always aware of its location and whether or not it is being wielded. For the purposes of locating her tool, she benefits from the Direction Sense merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 12-08-2016, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T10:29:48-08:00","id":1014371,"title":"","content":"This looks good. Is there a way for it to be applied with other types of tools? Like a staff or something equally long?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T10:32:18-08:00","id":1014372,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, there's no real reason why not. I'll edit it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T10:43:55-08:00","id":1014376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1014345#post1014345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see what you're suggesting work as the second-dot benefit so I can bump up the ability to redirect a countered spell with a Willpower expenditure to the third dot. How long would it last, though? For a scene? Or would it last a number of turns equal to the countering Mage's dots in the relevant Arcanum?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say scene. They can always just Scour the Condition if needed, but it will cost them, especially if you can keep applying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T10:52:53-08:00","id":1014377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1014376#post1014376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say scene. They can always just Scour the Condition if needed, but it will cost them, especially if you can keep applying it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great. Now, I just need to give names for each of the three benefits of the Spellbreaker style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T06:16:14-08:00","id":1014725,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Ruptor Cantaminis</u> (o to ooo, Style)<br /> Prerequisites:</b> Countermagic Stance, Wits 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You are highly profficient in a style of combat magic built around skill with the Counterspell Attainment. The name itself roughly means Spellbreaker in Latin, and practitioners are indeed capable of crippling their rivals' ability to cast their most powerful magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Oculus (o)</b> -- When countering the spells of another Mage, you are able to gain a measure of insight on whatever imago you are attempting to disrupt. Whenever you invoke the Counterspell Attainment, you may reflexively roll Wits + Gnosis vs. Gnosis + Composure. Each success in excess of the opposing character's allows you to learn one of the following information on the spell: Practice, Primary Factor, Spell Factors, Reach effects, and Withstand rating.<br /> <br /> <b>Signum (oo)</b> -- A successful Counterspell normally disrupts whatever magic is being cast by your opponent. However, you are able to strengthen this effect to further hinder a Mage in using a specific spell. When you succeed on a Counterspell roll, you may spend a Willpower point to inflict the Imago Retorta Condition keyed to the target spell for the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Repletio (ooo)</b> -- Mages must exercise caution in how they utilize their reserves of Mana, as it is integral to performing the most potent of spells. Your successful uses of the Counterspell Attainment allow you to replenish some of your energy by sapping it from the spells you disrupt. On a successful Counterspell roll, you gain half the Mana spent on the countered spell, rounded up.<br /> <br /> ---=---<br /> <b>New Condition: Imago Retorta</b><br /> Your character's ability to visualize a particular Imago is hobbled. Each time he attempts to use the associated spell, he suffers a dice penalty equal to the inflicting Mage's dots in the spell's primary Arcanum.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The mage successfully casts the affected spell.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> N/A.<br /> ---=---","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-09-2016, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T06:44:42-08:00","id":1014731,"title":"","content":"I would make Abruption reduce dice to the casting pool rather than reducing successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T06:47:20-08:00","id":1014733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1014731#post1014731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would make Abruption reduce dice to the casting pool rather than reducing successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should probably change the name, too, since I derived it from the Abruption Condition in Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T07:11:49-08:00","id":1014744,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of Latin names for Magical Styles, so I would call spellbreaker Ruptor Cantaminis (literally the same thing).<br /> <br /> If I had to name the abilities, I would also do cursory view -&gt; Oculus, arcane seal -&gt; Signum, and Magic Rod -&gt; Repletio.<br /> <br /> <b>New Condition: </b>Imago Retorta (<i>Twisted Image</i> in Latin)<br /> Your character's ability to visualize a particular Imago is hobbled. Each time he attempts to use the associated spell, he suffers a dice penalty equal to the Spellbreaker dots of the inflicting mage.<br /> Resolution: The mage successfully casts the affected spell.<br /> Beats: N/A.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T07:37:17-08:00","id":1014761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kvark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1014744#post1014744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a fan of Latin names for Magical Styles, so I would call spellbreaker Ruptor Cantaminis (literally the same thing).<br /> <br /> If I had to name the abilities, I would also do cursory view -&gt; Oculus, arcane seal -&gt; Signum, and Magic Rod -&gt; Repletio.<br /> <br /> <b>New Condition: </b>Imago Retorta (<i>Twisted Image</i> in Latin)<br /> Your character's ability to visualize a particular Imago is hobbled. Each time he attempts to use the associated spell, he suffers a dice penalty equal to the Spellbreaker dots of the inflicting mage.<br /> Resolution: The mage successfully casts the affected spell.<br /> Beats: N/A.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely helpful.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Thanks for this. I might make Ruptor Cantaminis one of the names used for Spellbreaker, and mention it as such in the description.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T18:09:51-08:00","id":1015049,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have an idea on how the scrapped Brutal Sorcery style could be homebrewed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T16:16:08-08:00","id":1015402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deions