ant.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T17:10:58-08:00","id":1015415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1015409#post1015409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly the same as anything else - with terrifying, <i>terrifying</i> madness and spewed glossolalia!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Brutal Sorcery [Style; \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022]</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Stamina \u2022\u2022\u2022, Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <i>Agony Ascendant</i> (\u2022): You may treat scouring your Pattern as a Yantra, with a bonus equal to your dots in this merit.<br /> <i>Pain to Perfection</i> (\u2022\u2022): You may choose to take an additional level of Resistant Lethal damage when scouring your pattern - if you do, you gain one Willpower.<br /> <i>Beauty in Screams </i>(\u2022\u2022\u2022): As long as you are suffering from Resistant Lethal damage, all damage dealt by your spells is also Resistant.</div> </div> </div> </div>amechra, you always make the best homebrew. Is it alright if I add some extra fluff to each of those benefits?<br /> <br /> Also, this would go pretty well with my conversion of the Body-Ravaging Magic Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-10-2016, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T17:52:56-08:00","id":1015428,"title":"","content":"As much as I hate it\u00b9, sure, go ahead and fluff them up a bit.<br /> <br /> \u00b9 I've been burned before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T18:36:01-08:00","id":1015454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1015428#post1015428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I hate it\u00b9, sure, go ahead and fluff them up a bit.<br /> <br /> \u00b9 I've been burned before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I'll be sure to credit you when I add it on the doc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T22:29:41-08:00","id":1016917,"title":"","content":"Added some extra fluff to amechra's Brutal Sorcery Merit. Critique is welcome for this.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Brutal Sorcery</u> [Style; \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022]</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Stamina \u2022\u2022\u2022, Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect:</b> By inflicting harm upon yourself, you can strengthen your magic in a manner that may overwhelm even an Awakened of greater skill in the Art.<br /> <br /> <b>Agony Ascendant (\u2022) --</b> Magic always has a price, and you pay that cost in blood in order to weave your spells more effectively. You may treat scouring your Pattern as a Yantra, with a bonus equal to your dots in this merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Pain to Perfection (\u2022\u2022) --</b> In the face of adversity, you find yourself instilled with the will to push forward. You may choose to take an additional level of Resistant Lethal damage when scouring your pattern - if you do, you gain one Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Beauty in Screams (\u2022\u2022\u2022) --</b> Pain is unavoidable, and that which cannot be healed through magic allows your spells to inflict the same. As long as you are suffering from Resistant Lethal damage, all damage dealt by your spells is also Resistant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T01:40:59-08:00","id":1016947,"title":"","content":"The second dot seems almost worthless. Almost all Mages can reliably refresh their entire Willpower pools by casting spells so there is no incentive to actually take that extra resistant Lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T01:49:41-08:00","id":1016949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1016917#post1016917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Added some extra fluff to amechra's Brutal Sorcery Merit. Critique is welcome for this.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>Brutal Sorcery</u> [Style; \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022]</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Stamina \u2022\u2022\u2022, Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect:</b> By inflicting harm upon yourself, you can strengthen your magic in a manner that may overwhelm even an Awakened of greater skill in the Art.<br /> <br /> <b>Agony Ascendant (\u2022) --</b> Magic always has a price, and you pay that cost in blood in order to weave your spells more effectively. You may treat scouring your Pattern as a Yantra, with a bonus equal to your dots in this merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Pain to Perfection (\u2022\u2022) --</b> In the face of adversity, you find yourself instilled with the will to push forward. You may choose to take an additional level of Resistant Lethal damage when scouring your pattern - if you do, you gain one Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Beauty in Screams (\u2022\u2022\u2022) --</b> Pain is unavoidable, and that which cannot be healed through magic allows your spells to inflict the same. As long as you are suffering from Resistant Lethal damage, all damage dealt by your spells is also Resistant.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the fist dot this follows the same restriction as standard scouring? It seems a bit weak when compared to gaining three mana. I agree with Tessie that the extra resistant lethal is not worth a willpower. As it is a single use of this yantra could take one day to recover. Now the third dot though I'm uncertain if it is balanced does give both thematic and mechanical reasons to use this style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T01:54:36-08:00","id":1016952,"title":"","content":"It's easy to step it up a notch, treat every point of Lethal damage (Up to dots in the Merit) you have as a Yantra that you can use until the damage is healed, and give a WP everytime you Scour along with the mana instead of charging an extra Lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T02:23:36-08:00","id":1016956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1016952#post1016952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's easy to step it up a notch, treat every point of Lethal damage (Up to dots in the Merit) you have as a Yantra that you can use until the damage is healed, and give a WP everytime you Scour along with the mana instead of charging an extra Lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like this?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Agony Ascendant (\u2022) --</b> Magic always has a price, and you pay that cost in blood in order to weave your spells more effectively. You treat every point of lethal damage you are suffering (up to a maximum equal to your dots in this Merit) as a Yantra bonus.<br /> <br /> <b>Pain to Perfection (\u2022\u2022) --</b> In the face of adversity, you find yourself instilled with the will to push forward. Whenever you scour your pattern for Mana, you also gain a Willpower point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T03:43:21-08:00","id":1016973,"title":"","content":"1) I'd personally make it any Resistant Lethal you're suffering since the intent seemed to be empowering your magic via Scouring. Maybe they can spend a mana to convert any Lethal they're suffering into Resistant in order to use it for their magic though. Basically, you want to circumvent any attempts to quickly gain powerful Yantras that don't come with a drawback. Regular Lethal is too easily healed, and would create an easy mechanic to exploit.<br /> <br /> 2) Yup, looks good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T06:56:39-08:00","id":1017037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1016973#post1016973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) I'd personally make it any Resistant Lethal you're suffering since the intent seemed to be empowering your magic via Scouring. Maybe they can spend a mana to convert any Lethal they're suffering into Resistant in order to use it for their magic though. Basically, you want to circumvent any attempts to quickly gain powerful Yantras that don't come with a drawback. Regular Lethal is too easily healed, and would create an easy mechanic to exploit.<br /> <br /> 2) Yup, looks good.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this, then? I imagine gaining resistant lethal damage could be done instead through my version of Body-Ravaging Magic.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Agony Ascendant (\u2022) -- </b>Magic always has a price, and you pay that cost in blood to weave your spells more effectively. You treat every point of resistant lethal damage you may suffer (up to a maximum equal to your dots in this Merit) as a Yantra bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-14-2016, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T07:17:31-08:00","id":1017050,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> The 3rd dot seems a bit powerful. One resistant damage and <i>all</i> of your spell damage becomes resistant? What about up to your dots in this merit (3, almost always), or only when you Scour or otherwise inflict resistant damage upon yourself? The math still favors you, since you can take 1 Resistant in exchange for dealing Potency in Resistant damage. <hr /><br /> Hmm. Would some Duration manipulation have a place in that Style? Like - take a point of Resistant damage (Bashing, Lethal, or Aggravated), and the spell you cast lasts as long as that point of Resistant damage (15 minutes for Bashing, 2 days for Lethal, etc.). Tradeoff is keeping damage on your track in exchange for longer spells - abusing this carries its own consequences. If you somehow heal the damage before schedule, the spell also ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-14-2016, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T08:10:45-08:00","id":1017072,"title":"","content":"<b>Fortified Sanctum (Style; \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sanctum \u2022+, Gnosis 3, Wits 3, Occult 3<br /> <br /> <b>(\u2022):</b> Your defenses are harder to dispel than normal. When assigning Reach to Advanced Potency, the spell\u2019s Withstand ability against dispellation increases by your dots in this Style, up to a total of +5.<br /> <br /> <b>(\u2022\u2022):</b> When your defenses are involved in a Clash Of Wills, you gain Successes equal to your Gnosis/2 round up or Successes rolled, whichever is higher.<br /> <br /> <b>(\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> When sacrificing a dot of Willpower to safely relinquish a spell to defend your Sanctum, you may halve all the penalties incurred by increased spell factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T08:18:27-08:00","id":1017079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1017050#post1017050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> The 3rd dot seems a bit powerful. One resistant damage and <i>all</i> of your spell damage becomes resistant? What about up to your dots in this merit (3, almost always), or only when you Scour or otherwise inflict resistant damage upon yourself? The math still favors you, since you can take 1 Resistant in exchange for dealing Potency in Resistant damage. <hr /><br /> Hmm. Would some Duration manipulation have a place in that Style? Like - take a point of Resistant damage (Bashing, Lethal, or Aggravated), and the spell you cast lasts as long as that point of Resistant damage (15 minutes for Bashing, 2 days for Lethal, etc.). Tradeoff is keeping damage on your track in exchange for longer spells - abusing this carries its own consequences. If you somehow heal the damage before schedule, the spell also ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or perhaps Willpower can be spent to make the spells resistant? Of course, that is my suggestion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T06:53:39-08:00","id":1029023,"title":"","content":"Regarding discussions on how Imbued Items work (specifically, their piddly dice-pools for low level spells when used by Sleeper/Sleepwalkers), which of these looks better?<br /> <br /> <b>Enchanted Proficiency (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker, Occult 2+<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Long, practiced, studied use of enchanted and ensorcelled paraphernalia has given you greater ability with using Imbued Items successfully. You made add your dots in this merit to the casting rolls for spells from Imbued Items.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> <b>Enchanted Proficiency (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker, Occult 2+<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Long, practiced, studied use of enchanted and ensorcelled paraphernalia has given you greater ability with using Imbued Items successfully. You get a +3 bonus on casting rolls for spells from Imbued Items with Arcana ratings equal to this merit or less.<br /> <br /> Option 1 applies to all Imbued casting rolls from the get-go, but starts very small. Option 2 give a nice, reliable static +3, but you need to get higher rating to use higher spells. One or two dots would be great for most users, with only those finding/using Adept and Master level Imbued Items needing the higher ratings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T07:12:41-08:00","id":1029035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1029023#post1029023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding discussions on how Imbued Items work (specifically, their piddly dice-pools for low level spells when used by Sleeper/Sleepwalkers), which of these looks better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dang. Both look pretty good mechanics-wise. If I had to pick, though, it would probably be Option 2 to keep them from readily using more powerful Imbued Items with greater efficiency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-09-2017, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T02:18:09-08:00","id":1031502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1017079#post1017079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or perhaps Willpower can be spent to make the spells resistant? Of course, that is my suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make it a Mana expenditure personally, not unlike using Mana to upgrade damage to aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T02:24:06-08:00","id":1031503,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Foci</u> (ooo)<br /> Prerequisites:</b> Wits 3, Occult 2<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have learned to focus your Mage Sight through a collection of tools, and thus open yourself to greater insights from a Mystery. So long as they can be semiotically linked to divination, revelation, or understanding, you may use any number of Path and Order tools as Yantras in Focused Mage Sight. When making any Revelation or Scrutiny rolls, the equipment bonus conferred by these Yantras cannot exceed +5.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> You must spend a turn to use each additional Yantra after the first in order to attune your Mage Sight to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Concerted Scrutiny</u> (o, ooo, ooooo)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Wits 3, Empathy 2<br /> <b>Effect:</b> When leading your fellow Mages in examining a given Mystery, you can harmonize their Nimbuses with yours to mitigate the likelihood of occult tampering. When using Focused Mage Sight as a teamwork action, you add half your dots in this Merit, rounded up, to the number of teamwork rolls that are counted as a single Scrutiny roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-15-2017, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:19:32-08:00","id":1031652,"title":"","content":"Agony Ascendant doesn't replace the Mana you gain from scouring - it just <i>also</i> gives you a bonus to spellcasting if you Scour while doing so.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Pain to Perfection's a bit of a bum trade - I think I'll swap that over to +1 Mana, +1 Willpower (so Scouring gives you 3mp for 1L(r), or 4mp 1wp for 2L(r), as well as a +2 Yantra if you incorporate it into your spells).<br /> <br /> My fault on Beauty In Screams - I actually have an alternative to that. Heck, I'll just replace the merit:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Brutal Sorcery [Style; \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022]</span><br /> <b>Agony Ascendant (\u2022) \u2014</b> You may Scour your Pattern as part of casting a spell. If you do so, you may claim a Yantra bonus equal to your dots in this merit in addition to any other benefits gained from Pattern Scouring.<br /> <b>Pain to Perfection (\u2022\u2022) \u2014</b> Whenever you Scour your Pattern, you may choose to take an additional level of Resistant Lethal damage. If you do so, you regain an additional point of Mana as well as a point of Willpower.<br /> <b>Beauty In Screams (\u2022\u2022\u2022) \u2014</b> You may forgo the normal 3 points of Mana gained from Scouring your Pattern when doing so as a Yantra. In exchange, you gain one additional free Reach for that spell, over and above the limit dictated by your dots in the appropriate Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:57:57-08:00","id":1031681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1031652#post1031652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...you gain one additional free Reach for that spell, over and above the limit dictated by your dots in the appropriate Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't do that, I'd set it up to reduce Paradox dice. You're using your pain like a dedicated tool after all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T04:39:10-08:00","id":1032080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1031681#post1031681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't do that, I'd set it up to reduce Paradox dice. You're using your pain like a dedicated tool after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second that. So a fixed -2 reduction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-f