e\">Agony Ascendant doesn't replace the Mana you gain from scouring - it just <i>also</i> gives you a bonus to spellcasting if you Scour while doing so.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Pain to Perfection's a bit of a bum trade - I think I'll swap that over to +1 Mana, +1 Willpower (so Scouring gives you 3mp for 1L(r), or 4mp 1wp for 2L(r), as well as a +2 Yantra if you incorporate it into your spells).<br /> <br /> My fault on Beauty In Screams - I actually have an alternative to that. Heck, I'll just replace the merit:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Brutal Sorcery [Style; \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022]</span><br /> <b>Agony Ascendant (\u2022) \u2014</b> You may Scour your Pattern as part of casting a spell. If you do so, you may claim a Yantra bonus equal to your dots in this merit in addition to any other benefits gained from Pattern Scouring.<br /> <b>Pain to Perfection (\u2022\u2022) \u2014</b> Whenever you Scour your Pattern, you may choose to take an additional level of Resistant Lethal damage. If you do so, you regain an additional point of Mana as well as a point of Willpower.<br /> <b>Beauty In Screams (\u2022\u2022\u2022) \u2014</b> You may forgo the normal 3 points of Mana gained from Scouring your Pattern when doing so as a Yantra. In exchange, you gain one additional free Reach for that spell, over and above the limit dictated by your dots in the appropriate Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this I may use it if you don't mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T05:28:57-08:00","id":1032096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1032091#post1032091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I dunno, Mystery Lenses? The Merit covers more than literal lenses, of course, but I think the name is still appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1032092#post1032092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe just Foci?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll go with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-15-2017, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T05:49:01-08:00","id":1032099,"title":"","content":"I'm really surprised no one's contributed a Merit like this in the thread (can't be the only one who's had the idea). Welp, here goes nothing:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bonded Tool (\u25cf to \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b></u><br /> The mage has a Tool with a will of its own, in a sense. While it cannot move or otherwise influence the world around it directly, it does have it's preferences for that particular mage when they work their magic through it, especially when said mage works to deepen the bond. When the Tool is used by any other mage, it bucks and kicks. It refuses to work properly, lessening its benefit and even being deleterious to wield.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> When used as a Yantra for the +1 bonus, add this Merit's dots to that bonus. This Merit may apply to any type of Tool, including Dedicated Tools. When the Tool is used by anyone other than the bonded mage, treat the Merit as half of its dots (rounded down) and the mage gains an appropriate Condition (examples below).<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The Tool has a Signature Nimbus, layering on top of the mage's own when spells are cast. In addition, the bond can be usurped by another mage. How this happens depends on the nature of both Tool and the original owner, but defeating the original owner in a Duel Arcane, the original owner misusing or abusing the Tool and then suddenly used by a mage who didn't, or even killing the original owner are common and well-known instances. If another mage usurps the Tool, this Merit is lost and the usurper gains it at 1 dot.<br /> <br /> Example Conditions<br /> <br /> <u><b>Overloaded</b></u><br /> (Kudos to rwknoll for the idea)<br /> The mage's Sight has been blinded by overwhelming sensitivity to the Supernal World. They can hardly look at it, let alone study the Mysteries. The mage must spend 1 Willpower just to engage Active Mage Sight (it does last for the rest of the scene, though). When using Focused Mage Sight for any Revelation or Scrutiny rolls on a Mystery, the player can opt to fail the roll to resolve this Condition, but the mage cannot do any more Revelation or Scrutiny rolls for that Mystery.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Dramatic failure on a Revelation or Scrutiny roll; using someone else's Bonded Tool<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Resolve as described above.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <br /> <u><b>Impotent</b></u><br /> The mage's willworking has suddenly dampened, making it easier for others to resist their magic. The Withstand rating on all Withstood spells increase by 1.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Successfully cast a Withstood spell; win a Duel Arcane<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <br /> <u><b>Found</b></u><br /> The Bonded Tool has alarmed its owner of the mage's meddling. The mage becomes paranoid, envisioning the owner bringing brutal vengeance upon them (even if said owner would never do so). The mage suffers a -2 penalty on Composure rolls to stay calm and lie about their paranoia.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The mage returns or submits the Bonded Tool to its owner<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:44:59-08:00","id":1035248,"title":"","content":"Having just read the Laundry RPG books, I'm thinking about adapting that style of sorcery and Computational Demonology to Mage, specifically invoking things like the Nemesis Continuum (IE Bad!Math that echoes from anti-reality) for achieving effects via induced (hopefully controlled*) Abyssal Intrusion.<br /> <br /> * = controlled being a loose term here, representing &quot;It mostly does what I want and hasn't eaten my face yet.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-20-2017, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:27:45-08:00","id":1037028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1035248#post1035248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having just read the Laundry RPG books, I'm thinking about adapting that style of sorcery and Computational Demonology to Mage, specifically invoking things like the Nemesis Continuum (IE Bad!Math that echoes from anti-reality) for achieving effects via induced (hopefully controlled*) Abyssal Intrusion.<br /> <br /> * = controlled being a loose term here, representing &amp;quot;It mostly does what I want and hasn't eaten my face yet.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me. I should probably look at the GURPs books I have and see what I can derive from them. On a different note....<br /> <hr /><br /> <b><u>Refined Practice</u> (o, ooo, or ooooo)</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Where most Awakened become versed in the use of certain spells, you have honed your approach of the Art around a specific purpose. Upon purchasing the Merit, choose a Practice within the limits of your Arcana. When casting a spell of that Practice, you gain free Reach equal to half your dots in this Merit, rounded up.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on this? I'm wondering if I should make this require Mana or Willpower, or whether to make it a prerequisite for (or even reimagine it as) a Style Merit that involves the Practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:34:41-08:00","id":1037032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1032099#post1032099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really surprised no one's contributed a Merit like this in the thread (can't be the only one who's had the idea). Welp, here goes nothing:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bonded Tool (\u25cf to \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b></u></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really promising concept. I kind of wonder if this is something that could result from a spell, like the Familiar Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T23:40:30-08:00","id":1037063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1037028#post1037028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That reminds me. I should probably look at the GURPs books I have and see what I can derive from them. On a different note.... <hr /><br /> <b><u>Refined Practice</u> (o, ooo, or ooooo)</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Where most Awakened become versed in the use of certain spells, you have honed your approach of the Art around a specific purpose. Upon purchasing the Merit, choose a Practice within the limits of your Arcana. When casting a spell of that Practice, you gain free Reach equal to half your dots in this Merit, rounded up.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on this? I'm wondering if I should make this require Mana or Willpower, or whether to make it a prerequisite for (or even reimagine it as) a Style Merit that involves the Practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incredibly powerful if used for the Master-level practices, which only get 1 free reach ever, by design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 01-24-2017, 03:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T00:05:46-08:00","id":1037069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1037063#post1037063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is incredibly powerful is used for the Master-level practices, which only get 1 free reach ever, by design.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about a 3 and 5 dot version which gives one and two Reach respectively*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T01:48:41-08:00","id":1037085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1037032#post1037032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a really promising concept. I kind of wonder if this is something that could result from a spell, like the Familiar Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I do try. As for making one, I think a Making Prime spell cast on an object should do the trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T02:27:02-08:00","id":1037096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1037069#post1037069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a 3 and 5 dot version which gives one and two Reach respectively*</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't. I think the caps on Reach should probably be absolute except in those rare situational circumstances like a demesne.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T03:51:01-08:00","id":1037115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1037096#post1037096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't. I think the caps on Reach should probably be absolute except in those rare situational circumstances like a demesne.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the existence of Rotes makes that limit a little more ignorable for anything except Master (and to a lesser extent, Adept) level magic. For everything else, there are options to increase your free Reach.<br /> <br /> For those two (especially Master), less Reach is a huge factor. If you want to reach beyond anything but Instant for a Master level spell, you're looking at a minimum of 3 Paradox, with 3 more for every additional Reach.<br /> <br /> @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\">Deionscribe</a> </b>I would value every additional Reach on Making/Unmaking as heavily as you value an effect that gives -3 Paradox. An effect that gives two free Reach is de-facto -6 Paradox on those Practices, or the equivalent of the ability to employ 3 Dedicated tools without taking any Yantra slots up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T05:02:36-08:00","id":1037126,"title":"","content":"I consider Rotes to be a rare situational circumstance since they don't cover all your magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T05:22:59-08:00","id":1037130,"title":"","content":"Worth remembering also that rotes also don't actually expand your capacity beyond what is attainable by a normal (but powerful) Mage.<br /> <br /> Extra Reach would be a fun thing for a very rare, very specific rote to grant, though, especially at the Master level; it'd see some <i>very</i> powerful Mages get into a pissing match.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T05:27:42-08:00","id":1037131,"title":"","content":"I figure if you can track down an archmaster and get a Rote off him you'd get his level of Reach, or maybe a Rank 5 Supernal entity could teach a Rote that has extra Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:12:08-08:00","id":1037149,"title":"","content":"That would be the sort of action worthy of it, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T00:18:03-08:00","id":1037699,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Focal Point</u> (ooo)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sanctum<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Not only can your Sanctum serve as an anchor for some of your spells, but its sympathetic ties to your soul allows you to further focus your imago. When casting a spell within the Sanctum, you may incorporate a number of extra Yantras equal to its dot rating. This Merit can be purchased multiple times, with each applied to another Sanctum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T06:42:46-08:00","id":1037805,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Sanctified Tool</u> (o to ooo)</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Whenever you use a Dedicated Tool keyed to this Merit, it inflicts an additional penalty equal to its dot rating on any Paradox rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Invoking this benefit in a casting roll is counted to the number of Yantras you can use based on your Gnosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T07:43:47-08:00","id":1043544,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Extensa(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Style)</span></span></b></span> <hr /><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Resolve (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">), Composure(</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The ancient art of losing yourself in your Imago. Some call it Spellzerk.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Iron Will (\u2022)</b>: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By repeated training mage is able hone his focusing skill. Concentration Yantra now grants +3 modifier for him (instead of +2).</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No Interference (\u2022\u2022):</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> If you win CoW you can spend WP to apply <b>Crushed Condition</b> on your enemy.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>One With The Imago (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At this level willworker can benefit from All-Out Attack maneuver even while spellcasting. Sacrificing defence grants another +2 modifier when he uses Concentration Yantra that stacks with Iron Will. </span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Unshakable (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every turn spent on Concentration gives +1 to CoW on this spell. This bonus cannot go higher then rating of used Arcana but an overall modifier can go beyond +5</span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Crushed</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your character has not only lost in a Clash of Wills but was crushed by opponents immense force and made completely open and exposed to him. For the duration of this Condition, the character cannot spend Willpower or use magic in any way to harm the mage or spells she was defeated by. Further, the mage who won the CoW has Strong sympathy with the loser.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resolution:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This Condition lingers until you step back and take your time cool down and think what went wrong - this requires at least an hour of Meditation. Or until the winner of the CoW takes advantage of the sympathy in a way that injures or abuses the loser. Take a Beat.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Beat:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Retreat</span></span></div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What do you think?</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T08:04:01-08:00","id":1043557,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> <br /> This is pretty interesting. It makes the Concentration Yantra more useful in spellcasting, I hope you don't mind if I add more text and do some corrections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T08:06:21-08:00","id":1043558,"title":"","content":"I don't mind. Actually I'm looking forward to it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's a first draft so all input is appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T08:31:55-08:00","id":1043570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1043558#post1043558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind. Actually I'm looking forward to it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's a first draft so all input is appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><u>Extensa</u> (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Style)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Resolve 3, Composure 3<br /> <b>Effect: </b>You have become profficient in the art of losing yourself in your Imago. While this can leave you vulnerable, especially in the heat of battle, it can make your magic stronger and more difficult to overcome.<br /> <br /> <u>Willful Intent</u> (\u2022) -- Through repeated training, you have honed your ability to focus on the aim of a given spell. Whenever you employ the Concentration Yantra, it now grants a +3 bonus instead of +2.<br /> <br /> <u>No Interference</u> (\u2022\u2022) -- You possess a strong force of will, and it can easily overpower those who would oppose your magic by supernatural means. If you win a Clash of Wills triggered against your spell, you can spend Willpower to apply the Crushed Condition on your enemy. This maneuver cannot be used if Willpower was spent earlier in the turn.<br /> <br /> <u>One With The Imago</u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022): By diverting your full attention to the spell, you can further refine its effects. At this level, you can benefit from the All-Out Attack maneuver even while spellcasting. Sacrificing Defense grants a +2 dice bonus. This can stack with the added bonus of Willful Intent.<br /> <br /> <u>Unshakable</u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): You can now empower your magic so that it cannot be easily contested either by fellow Awakened or other supernaturals. Every turn spent on Concentration gives a +1 bonus to the Clash of Wills on the spell. This extra bonus cannot go higher then the rating of the Primary Arcanum, but it can bring the overall modifier beyond +5.<br /> <br /> ---=---<br /> <u><b>Crushed</b></u><br /> Your character has not only lost a Clash of Wills, but was also crushed by his opponent's immense force, thus being left completely open and exposed to him. For the duration of this Condition, you cannot spend Willpower or use supernatural powers in any way to harm the inflicting character. Furthermore, the mage who won the Clash has Strong sympathy towards you.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution:</b> This Condition lingers until you step back and take your time to cool down and think what went wrong. This requires at least an hour of Meditation, or until the winner of the Clash of Wills takes advantage of the sympathy in a way that injures or abuses the loser.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat:</b> You retreat from your opponent.<br /> ---=---","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 02-04-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T08:43:14-08:00","id":1043576,"title":"","content":"The verbiage about being aware of the Clash is unnecessary, Mages are explicitly always aware when one of their spells Clashes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T08:48:08-08:00","id":1043579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1043576#post1043576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The verbiage about being aware of the Clash is unnecessary, Mages are explicitly always aware when one of their spells Clashes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Thanks for mentioning that. Will revise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T09:22:57-08:00","id":1043597,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> Thanks for cleaning up the language. I always struggle with english translations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T15:58:27-08:00","id":1043760,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Cast and Go </u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mind (\u2022) </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>or </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life (\u2022) </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>or </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">none?, Composure 3, Athletics 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Effect:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Running is simple, based on instincts. You can keep your mind clear and take both running and casting action in the same turn. Doing so leaves you open for mundane attacks, you lose your Defence.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 02-04-2017, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T11:59:08-08:00","id":1044118,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Insightful Familiar </b></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Familiar (any type)</span></b><br /> <b>Effect: </b>Your familiar knows things. Things that would surprise you. A thousand remembered conversations heard from twilight, secrets seen in the shadow, weird conjunctions observed in astral space - all these things stay with your familiar, and sometimes one thing reminds it of another, and it has useful advise. <br /> <br /> It isn't necessarily clear. Ghost can have very spotty memories, spirits don't think like humans, and a goetia's ability to ponder on things is limited by its own focus, but they can give useful tidbits.<br /> You are likely always asking your familiar questions, but once per chapter you can ask it something you really need an answer to, and it will remember to delve into that weird backlog of lore it keeps in its ephemeral mind. You may ask it up (dot ranking) yes or no questions about a topic, and it will answer.<br /> <br /> This is basically the Dream merit retooled to work with familiars. I like the dream merit, but don't really think it is appropriate for most non-Mastigos mages. Plus I wanted my familiar to be more of an advisor.<br /> Obviously the storyteller plays the part of the familiar as it racks its little head (or equivalent) to answer your questions.<br /> The player (not necessarily the character) decides when one of his (potentially frantic) questions actually taps this well of knowledge, though the storyteller may decide to help the player out by just deciding to let it kick in. It is more convenient than Dream (no sleep or mediation needed) but suffers from more potential limitations based on the familiars nature. A ghost is never likely to know something that requires current information on activity in the Shadow, for instance.<br /> <br /> How workable do you think this will be?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T15:23:10-08:00","id":1044217,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar532_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"532\" data-vbnamecard=\"532\">Newes</a> Seems fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T15:59:59-08:00","id":1044243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1044217#post1044217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Seems fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I imagine I could fold the Daemon Merit into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T03:28:40-08:00","id":1057982,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Unlock Senses </u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life (\u2022) <i>or </i>none?, Wits 3</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> By embracing animal nature of your body you can use it to your advantage and aid Scrutiny and Revelation rolls. Sight, smell, sound, touch and taste are all connected. Every sense above first used in a study adds cumulative +1 to roll but also lengthens the interval by one turn. Phenomena must emit sound, have texture, scent, flavor or be visible in order to be perceived by corresponding senses.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Directed PMS </u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022 or \u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wits 3, Occult 2</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Willworker can assess the general direction from from which the trigger of PMS occurred e.g. \u201cin front of you\u201d, \u201con your left\u201d, \u201cbehind you\u201d or \u201cabove you\u201d. Two dot version allows him to pinpoint phenomena with astounding precision e.g. \u201cthis guy\u201d, \u201cthis table\u201d, \u201cthis wind\u201d.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Vigil </u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wits 3, Fate 1</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When your PMS is triggered you can sense if the effect is beneficial, neutral or negative to you. If if the fate of the effect or its cause is occluded you will receive \u201cneutral\u201d result without possibility of CoW. Four dot version lets you Clash with Gnosis + Fate.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":".  can't english 03-04-2017, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T06:10:16-08:00","id":1058015,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar532_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"532\" data-vbnamecard=\"532\">Newes</a>, I added your Insightful Familiar Merit, with a more polished writeup.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a>,your latest contributions are also interesting. I'll get back to this at a later date, though, seeing as I am catching up on other posts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 03-04-2017, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T07:23:41-08:00","id":1058034,"title":"","content":"Moinen, that's actually some pretty great stuff. I might even integrate them into my games. My only quibble is with Unlock Senses. It might be better to just say that the Mage can buy the merit for one dot and choose one of their senses which they can use to enhance their Mage Sight for a +1, all of which should require the Mage to get up close to and extensively handle their target. That way, it provides a direct mechanical benefit for some assumption of risk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T08:02:07-08:00","id":1058038,"title":"","content":"Thank you. And, um, you might be right about Unlock Senses. Changing it into a set of Unlock (Sense) merits might be better but then... you'll end up paying 5 merit points for for a whole set, which is too much for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T08:22:09-08:00","id":1058046,"title":"","content":"You could always just make it a general &quot;Let them use whichever sense they like&quot; for the +1 but it really shouldn't be more powerful than a +1. Otherwise, you'll find pretty quick that a novice Mage can brute-force a Mystery by rubbing themselves against it in an uncomfortably erotic manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T09:05:15-08:00","id":1058058,"title":"","content":"A novice mage can already brute force the Mystery. I find it ridiculous that Prime Unveiling or Perfecting couldn't grant dice bonus and trick to a Revelation and Scrutiny rolls. Sure they it can. Magic is a shortcut, and Prime is a shortcut to magical activities. It's in even in its purview: Revelation. And because of that I don't mind that non-Prime users could do it too.<br /> <br /> And yea, in my campaign I had a free 'lose your dignity by snifing and tongue clicking' to get a +1 to these rolls but nobody did it since I painted it as low and unworthy. So maybe just add some fluff bits or even a socialize stigma drawback?<br /> <br /> Edit: But if at your table you don't have such Prime spells you might be better with 1 dot 1 sense version of this merit. Whatever works for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-04-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T09:09:28-08:00","id":1058059,"title":"","content":"Umm... Moinen?<br /> <br /> You <i>do</i> know what PMS is a standard acronym for in English, right? I know you mean &quot;Passive Mage Sight&quot;, but...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T09:16:39-08:00","id":1058060,"title":"","content":"'Peripheral' and yup, I know. It's actually used in my country too but who cares, meh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T10:41:58-08:00","id":1058090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1058059#post1058059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm... Moinen?<br /> <br /> You <i>do</i> know what PMS is a standard acronym for in English, right? I know you mean &quot;Passive Mage Sight&quot;, but...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's more than one person who uses the acronym and everyone knows what it stands for, especially considering context. It's not an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T10:47:20-08:00","id":1058092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1058058#post1058058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A novice mage can already brute force the Mystery. I find it ridiculous that Prime Unveiling or Perfecting couldn't grant dice bonus and trick to a Revelation and Scrutiny rolls. Sure they it can. Magic is a shortcut, and Prime is a shortcut to magical activities. It's in even in its purview: Revelation. And because of that I don't mind that non-Prime users could do it too.<br /> <br /> And yea, in my campaign I had a free 'lose your dignity by snifing and tongue clicking' to get a +1 to these rolls but nobody did it since I painted it as low and unworthy. So maybe just add some fluff bits or even a socialize stigma drawback?<br /> <br /> Edit: But if at your table you don't have such Prime spells you might be better with 1 dot 1 sense version of this merit. Whatever works for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Prime can definitely help you but it doesn't make it guaranteed to work and, indeed, can make it more difficult. I'd say that Prime can't hand out dice bonuses because Scrutiny is not the act of discerning Truth from a Lie but rather to find which Truths you want from a big ol' bucket of them. Prime works to let you tell Truth apart but finding a specific Truth is trickier.<br /> <br /> Prime helps, instead, by doing things like the Light under a Bushel spell in the Signs preview. It gives you the ability to work a bit longer and provide better results, but a novice Mage isn't going to be unraveling grand Mysteries created by Archmasters, no matter how many shiny spells they have (though they might certainly get further and get more partial info).<br /> <br /> But, as you say, whatever works for you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T12:09:03-08:00","id":1058108,"title":"","content":"I was looking at Gnosis 1 and Gnosis 3 and I had an incredible feeling of suffering; playing a Mage Pre-Gnosis 3 looks like suffering where all you want to do is to get Gnosis 3 ASAP for extra Obsession, three times quicker Ritual Casting Intervals and a Combined Spell feature. This make me depressed, because while low Gnosis should have different gameplay feel to mid Gnosis, this is so brutal that it makes racing towards Gnosis 3 like a desperate speed bump.<br /> <br /> So I was thinking...what if there was some kind of Merit that can temporarily bridge the gap and let you pretend you are Gnosis 3 for certain aspects of Gnosis table? Something like this:<br /> <br /> ON ROAD TO GNOSIS / APPRENTICESHIP / WHATEVER ( 1 - 4 )<br /> This Merit represents you trying to be a good adult mage while still a cub. You can buy following options in any order you want.<br /> O: You gain &quot;Mage in Training&quot; Condition. It gives you a Beat each time you suffer from your state of still-incomplete Mage, and becomes resolved when you attain Gnosis 3.<br /> O: Your Ritual Casting Interval becomes 1,5 hour<br /> O: Your maximum number of Obssesions becomes 2<br /> O: You gain a third Yantra slot, which can be only used to incorporate your Dedicated Tool into the casting<br /> <br /> Note that these things lock you into specific values instead of giving you &quot;+1&quot;? That's because my intent is something like that: you pick these merits as a reflection of your Awakened training, and when you become Adult Enough to get into Gnosis 3 and gain these *for real*, you get XP invested in this back.<br /> This is an idea fueled by my fever and sickness, so I have no idea if I will hate it tomorrow, but I wonder what people think about it. I won't lie, I just don't like how oppressive is Ritual Casting interval pre-Gnosis 3, because I feel that newbies *should* rely heavily on ritual magic to do the heavy working, but in practice I never saw anyone in game decide to do that, because fuck, doing a Runic Circle Ritual takes 6 hours. Add a Grimoir Casting and it becomes 12! In these 6 hours, Gnosis 3 Mage can:<br /> - Do the Runic Circle and smuggle in 5 &quot;+1&quot; Ritual Intervals, making turning &quot;+2 dice because of better Gnosis&quot; edge into &quot;+7 because of Gnosis and Ritual Power&quot;! (or +10, because they can also get an extra yantra in)<br /> - Do the Runic Circle, smuggle in 2 &quot;+1&quot; Ritual Intervals, and still do a Grimoire thing<br /> - Cast the spell 6 times, which means they can just use all the dice on Factors and brute force that 1 (or chance) die into working simply by trying enough times.<br /> <br /> The massive time sink investment into Ritual Casting for a pre-gnosis 3 Mage makes it really unattractive option that you play safe, simply because not rolling it good makes you feel like an idiot who just wasted half a day trying to save one Reach and maybe get 2 dice more into your spellcasting, at which point you probably will never try it again and rely on your instant magic until you get to Gnosis 3 land of feeling like complete wizard.<br /> <br /> /rant, sorry for it, im sickier than usual<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> You probably could do something similar for &quot;Order Training&quot;, where you can slowly apply &quot;having an Order&quot; benefit to a character that doesn't have them, allowing you to model apprenticeship in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-04-2017, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T12:21:04-08:00","id":1058110,"title":"","content":"Hmm. This is making me consider a Virtuous/Vice-Ridden style Merit which gives you extra Obsession. One at two dots and another at four dots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T14:37:52-08:00","id":1058151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1058090#post1058090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's more than one person who uses the acronym and everyone knows what it stands for, especially considering context. It's not an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually bringing it up because it amuses me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T16:22:02-08:00","id":1060692,"title":"","content":"I was asked how being Mentored by a Supernal Being would look mechanically. Any idea if Mentor / Infamous Mentor merits are good to go with little reskinning, or do they need some bigger tweaks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T07:30:57-08:00","id":1060867,"title":"","content":"As suggested, I checked out Deionscribe's merits for Runes. Hmmm. Glyph Lore is interesting, but I'm not sure if it's balanced. A potential +3 [ending up with +5 yantra] for one merit dot sounds really strong. On the other hand, Runes are very niche and getting them to work reliably is a massive Batman like gambit. Got any practical experience with the merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T00:53:18-08:00","id":1061158,"title":"","content":"Question for Ravaging Magic: should it be considered a Yantra? I feel that making it a Yantra but allowing it to be used Reflexively in conjuction with another Yantra would give it an interesting niche [get to your power limit faster] instead of pushing the power limit by basically making it a yantra that doesn't use up Yantra slots. Hmm. This would also make it less cheesy for situations where that Bashing damage is irrelevant because it can be walked out...<br /> Maybe I should make the bashing option respect Yantra limits but be super fast, and add Lethal Resitant option that can bypass one Yantra limit? Resitant Lethal Damage isn't something you can spam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-11-2017, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T13:07:33-07:00","id":1062942,"title":"","content":"Original<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hammer </u>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resolve 3, Gnosis 3</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You prefer releasing Paradox instead of containing. And you are good at it. Substract dots in this merit from Paradox penalty to spells dice pool if released.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">???</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I feel like this could be a whole style.</span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Edit:</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Four Rules </u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Style)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resolve 3, Gnosis 3</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You prefer releasing Paradox instead of containing. And you are good at it. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Drawback:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">???</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Anchor</u> (\u2022) - Substract dots in this merit from Paradox penalty to spells dice pool if released.<br /> <u>Anchor</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> v2 (\u2022) - Halve Paradox penalty to spells dice pool if released. Round down.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>xxxxxx</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022) - </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>xxxxxx </u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022) - </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hammer</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) - After ST rolled for Paradox you can spend Mana to cancel his successes with one-to-one ratio. You have do it in one turn and you are still limited by Gnosis and dots in this merit.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-16-2017, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T15:22:39-07:00","id":1062997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1062942#post1062942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hammer </u>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resolve 3, Gnosis 3</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You prefer releasing Paradox instead of containing. And you are good at it. Substract dots in this merit from Paradox penalty to spells dice pool if released.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">???</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I feel like this could be a whole style.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>How about the Drawback is that your released Paradoxes last one step longer on the duration table?<br /> So an Understanding character's Paradoxes would last for One Story/Month, while a Falling character would release like a Mad One, with durations of One Chronicle/Year.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T16:20:25-07:00","id":1063016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1062942#post1062942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hammer </u>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resolve 3, Gnosis 3</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You prefer releasing Paradox instead of containing. And you are good at it. Substract dots in this merit from Paradox penalty to spells dice pool if released.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">???</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I feel like this could be a whole style.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>If you do a style with it, would you do it as a combat, social, or utility aspect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T16:46:31-07:00","id":1063021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1062997#post1062997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about the Drawback is that your released Paradoxes last one step longer on the duration table?<br /> So an Understanding character's Paradoxes would last for One Story/Month, while a Falling character would release like a Mad One, with durations of One Chronicle/Year.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about distributing it through your Nimbus and/or Sympathetic Connections?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T17:06:32-07:00","id":1063032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1063021#post1063021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about distributing it through your Nimbus and/or Sympathetic Connections?</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of releasing it that it affects your spell and the world, so having it affect your nimbus is counterintuitive.<br /> And releasing your Paradox through your sympathetic connections? That's even worse than just releasing randomly, you're actively buying a merit which can send Gulmoths off at family members.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T19:30:53-07:00","id":1063090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1063032#post1063032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point of releasing it that it affects your spell and the world, so having it affect your nimbus is counterintuitive.<br /> And releasing your Paradox through your sympathetic connections? That's even worse than just releasing randomly, you're actively buying a merit which can send Gulmoths off at family members.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T04:28:24-07:00","id":1063177,"title":"","content":"I'll get back to Hammer ( I edited the previous post) but in the meanwhile...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Practice Mastery</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Style)</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gnosis 3, Access to a Practice</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Effect:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You have devoted yourself to a single Practice. Merit doesn\u2019t work with Rotes since they have no place for your artistry. Praxis are compatible. Can be taken multiple times, each for a different practice.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Specialty</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022) -- Choose a Specialty in a Practice. When using it you benefit from usual +1 dice. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>So Below</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022) -- The mage can stabilize a spell by putting a chunk of the Supernal Realms strength. Spend 1 Mana to grant Advanced Potency.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Deeper Studies</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022\u2022) -- Deep understanding of a Practice allows him to always be aware of changes he can make in the surrounding world. It allows him to cast a spell reflexively at the cost of 1 Reach. He can\u2019t use Yantras that are not reflexive when doing so. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Mastery</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) -- Mage achieves full proficiency in spinning his spells. When it encounters the will of others Mage gets +1 to CoW</span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-16-2017, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T04:34:45-07:00","id":1063178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1062942#post1062942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Original<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hammer </u>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resolve 3, Gnosis 3</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You prefer releasing Paradox instead of containing. And you are good at it. Substract dots in this merit from Paradox penalty to spells dice pool if released.</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">???</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I feel like this could be a whole style.</span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Edit:</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Four Rules </u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Style)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resolve 3, Gnosis 3</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You prefer releasing Paradox instead of containing. And you are good at it. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Drawback:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">???</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Anchor</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022) - Substract dots in this merit from Paradox penalty to spells dice pool if released.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>xxxxxx</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022) - </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>xxxxxx </u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022) - </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hammer</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) - After ST rolled for Paradox you can spend Mana to cancel his successes with one-to-one ratio. You have do it in one turn and you are still limited by Gnosis and dots in this merit.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Instead of making the first dot benefit scale with the Merit, I would make it flat &quot;halve the Paradox penalty&quot;. Why? Because it gives you the biggest buff when you would release a gigantic paradox, of course, so if you want to get the most out of your buck...<br /> It also doesn't trivialize small Paradoxes.<br /> I also really like the idea of making Magical Styles follow a rule like this: &quot;Maximum number of dots you can have in this Style is equal to your Gnosis.&quot;<br /> Makes it grow with you, and allows some extra balancing possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-16-2017, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T05:07:57-07:00","id":1063183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1063178#post1063178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead of making the first dot benefit scale with the Merit, I would make it flat &quot;halve the Paradox penalty&quot;. Why? Because it gives you the biggest buff when you would release a gigantic paradox, of course, so if you want to get the most out of your buck...<br /> It also doesn't trivialize small Paradoxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if it's a good idea. I mean it's still a great boost for a one dot(and matches with Paradox theme nicely) but I feel like it's not enough carrot for a stick that the ST has with the Reach modifying.<br /> I added your idea to the merit<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also really like the idea of making Magical Styles follow a rule like this: &quot;Maximum number of dots you can have in this Style is equal to your Gnosis.&quot;<br /> Makes it grow with you, and allows some extra balancing possibilities. </div> </div> </div>I can see why but I prefer 'skill over power' take where you can develop horizontally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T03:46:09-07:00","id":1068230,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>In the Night </u>(\u2022 </span></b><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">to</span></b><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> \u2022\u2022, Style)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Status (GotV)</span><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> \u2022</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, Resolve </span><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, Time </span><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(for two dot effect)</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Breeze</u> (\u2022) Constant focus allows to react and hide signals your spell give under a different signal. Whenever your character registers a PMS ping it can cast in the very same moment a reflexive spell that won't be registered by PMS. Mana and Reach must be paid normally.<br /> <br /> <u>Steady Wind</u> (\u2022</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">) Extending senses in time allows to cast instant spell instead of a reflexive one. (Requires Time \u2022 )</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T05:33:12-07:00","id":1068260,"title":"","content":"I glanced over the google doc, but a quick question - <br /> <br /> Any new FC-type merits added in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T18:56:32-07:00","id":1068507,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Legacy Membership </u>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites:</b></span><b> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gnosis</span><b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> \u2022\u2022 </span></b></b> <i>Character Generation only; character must qualify for the Legacy in question</i><br /> <br /> Your character is an initiated member of a Legacy. For one dot version of this merit, they command knowledge of Legacy's first Attainment; for two dots version, they are capable of using Legacy's second attainment.<br /> If a player loses any of their Praxes due to Legacy rules, they may choose to either gain 1 Arcane XP+1 Arcane Beat as normal (with the possibility of spending it at character generation), or decide to keep the Praxis while still gaining 1 Arcane Beat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something to give &quot;start at Gnosis 2&quot; it's own niche, and give a easy way to make &quot;already in a Legacy&quot; chargen characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T02:10:55-07:00","id":1068585,"title":"","content":"I do find it interesting that combining the Illumination proximus merit with the Wise Sleepwalker proximus merit allows a proximus to come close to being a mage concerning mysteries. Perhaps acquiring these two merits in addition to 5 arcane xp is necessary for a proximus to awaken? That'd be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T06:01:22-07:00","id":1068629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1068260#post1068260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I glanced over the google doc, but a quick question -<br /> <br /> Any new FC-type merits added in?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For FC-aligned Sleepers, there is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=949458#post949458\">Traditional Understanding</a>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8180\" data-vbnamecard=\"8180\">Deionscribe</a> The Google docs seem a bit outdated, considering all the material here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T06:42:50-07:00","id":1068645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1068629#post1068629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> For FC-aligned Sleepers, there is <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=949458#post949458&amp;quot;]Traditional</a> Understanding[/URL].<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> The Google docs seem a bit outdated, considering all the material here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do need to update it, again. Been busy for a while because of work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T09:35:34-07:00","id":1079835,"title":"","content":"Is there a Merit for increasing the amount of Spell Control a Proximus has? If there isn't, does such a Merit have value?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T11:58:58-07:00","id":1079914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1079835#post1079835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a Merit for increasing the amount of Spell Control a Proximus has? If there isn't, does such a Merit have value?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make it cost two dots of merit per additiona spell slot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T18:37:17-07:00","id":1080123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1079914#post1079914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would make it cost two dots of merit per additiona spell slot.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, 2 or 4 dots for 2 or 3 spell control, respectively?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T21:48:02-07:00","id":1083833,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Spell Control</u> (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Proximus, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You are better able to manage control of your Blessings, and can keep more than one active at once. At 2 dots, you can increase your Spell Control by 1, and increase it by 1 again at 4 dots.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: A little something to give Proximi some breathing room when it comes to Spell Control.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Mystic Tools</u> (\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022, or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Proximus, Wits 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have learned how to utilize various mystically important devices, conditions, and methods to improve your Blessings. You can utilize 1 Yantra at 1 dot, 2 Yantras at 3 dots, and 3 Yantras at 5 dots.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Now Proximi can get in on the wand-waving, and bolstering their spell casting dice pools.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Attaining Insight</u> (Style, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Proximus, Occult 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> In depth studies have led to new insights into the nature of your gifts, granting you Attainments within a select Arcana.<br /> <i>The Sight (\u2022)</i>: You now have access to Passive and Active Mage Sight within the selected Arcana.<br /> <i>The Rebuke (\u2022\u2022)</i>: You can now have the Counterspell Attainment for the selected Arcana, except all uses require a point of Mana.<br /> <i>The Shield (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i>: You now have access to the selected Arcana's Mage Armor Attainment, fixed as if they had 2 dots in the relevant Arcana.<br /> <i>The Scroll (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i>: You now have access to the Lesser Utility Attainment for the selected Arcana.<br /> <i>The Call (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</i>: You can now summon a Supernal Entity (as per the Summoning rules on page 95), except the summoned Supernal Entity only has the selected Arcana. Roll Willpower for the summoning, and treat Gnosis as 1 for relevant rolls and effects (such as Abyssal interference).<br /> <b>Note:</b> A Proximus can select this merit once for each of their Blessing Arcana - each instance applies separately.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Access to Attainments, now in Proximus flavor. Helps cover up a few gaps in their Mage- skill set.]<br /> <br /> <b><u>Rote Sorcery</u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker, Occult 1, Occult Specialty in Awakened lore<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your studies have enabled you to replicate, if only barely, the effects of pre-encoded Supernal magic. You can now use and learn Rotes, despite not being Awakened or possessing the ability to cast the spells improvised. Spells have the default ritual casting time of 5 hours. Additionally, you can utilize one Yantra per dot in Occult for the casting of the Rote, and spend a point of Reach to add +2 dice to the spell casting pool.<br /> <b>Note:</b> Lacking Gnosis and Arcana ratings, your dice pool for casting any Rotes is limited only to what Yantras you can incorporate. While you benefit from the free Reach of the Rote, your lack of Arcana means all spell factors start at their default value of 1. Any additional Mana costs still have to be paid normally (such as through Cup Bearer, being a Proximus, using Tass or a Sacrament, etc.). You incur 1 Paradox die per exceeded Reach.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Now non-Mages can use Awakened magic... provided they've read the manual, and have enough modifiers to even make the attempt. Seriously, no free spell factor increases and a piddling dice pool means this merit won't be outshining real Mages any time soon. Nevermind having to get one's hands on Rotes to begin with.] <hr /><br /> Note, the Proximus ones above largely are (or make) redundant the Dynastic Heir (original recipe) merit chain, and Arcana-Strewn Nature and/or Illumination. These would be for those who prefer more a la carte enhancements. Or just different options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-27-2017, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:02:04-07:00","id":1084535,"title":"","content":"Related Idea to Rote Sorcery<br /> <br /> <b>Abyssal Sorcery (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Fitful Slumber, Occult 1, Occult Specialty in Abyssal lore<br /> <b>Effects:</b> The trauma left by the Abyss has scarred your soul... and opened your mind. You can learn Rotes (and antinomian Rotes), and can force them into reality despite not being Awakened yourself. The base ritual casting time is 5 hours, you can utilize one Yantra per dot in Occult for the casting of the Rote, and each Reach adds 1 Paradox die. Unlike with normal Rotes, you don't get free Reach - instead, all castings roll Paradox, but you can control as many Paradox successes as you would have had free Reach. If you score less successes on the Paradox roll, you only have that much Reach to use. Any Reach over your free allotment is handled normally.<br /> <b>Note:</b> Lacking Gnosis and Arcana ratings, your dice pool for casting any Rotes is limited only to what Yantras you can incorporate. Any additional Mana costs still have to be paid normally (such as through Cup Bearer, using Tass, etc.).<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: For Bargain Bin Abyssal Sorcerers to throw at your Mages. Note the interplay with Reach - you can use the Rote's &quot;free&quot; Reach Safely, but the total amount is determined by the Paradox roll. Too few dice, and you don't have much to play with, while adding in too many risks the spell escaping from you on a good roll.<br /> <br /> I probably need to add in more advantages to justify the massive gamble like nature of its use. Maybe rate the Merit 1 to 5, with each dot offering another &quot;controlled&quot; Reach?]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-09-2017, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T06:12:23-07:00","id":1093636,"title":"","content":"<b><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Shifter</span></span></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Life 1, Stamina 3</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Effect:</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some of those who signed their names on the Watchtower did this not with a hand but with a paw. When taking this Merit choose an animal that the mage can change into(him and only him). At 2 dots you gain access to spells that grant features of this particular animal one dot earlier - you still use your normal dice pool and stats, though. </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Example: </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Choosing a carp lets you change into this fish at 3rd dot of Life (with Shapechanging) or give yourself gills at 2nd dot. In both options you don\u2019t get the free reach since you are using practice higher then your own.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With the 3 dot version the mage is particularly comfortable in the animal forms he assumes, and his magic lasts longer than other mages who lack his mastery of shapeshifting. A mage with this Merit can worry less about awkwardly timed transformations back to human form (while the mage is flying as an eagle, for example), and he need not worry about the strain of repeated casting under circumstances where recasting a spell might be difficult. Add 2 steps on your Duration ladder for the purpose of those spells. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At 4th dot of this Merit understanding of his inner animal is even greater and mage can now assume his chosen animal form 2 dots earlier. In this case you must pay 1 Reach just to be able to cast those spells.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> It's a nod to those poor bastards who want to change forms but can't because of the need to wait for 4th dot. It's obvious and vulgar magic that is hard to use and you often have other, more useful spells to cast. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-17-2017, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T11:36:57-07:00","id":1093719,"title":"","content":"I could possibly see that in 1e where no one paid attention to the Practices, but in 2e I wouldn't let that fly at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T11:50:51-07:00","id":1093723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1093719#post1093719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could possibly see that in 1e where no one paid attention to the Practices, but in 2e I wouldn't let that fly at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I know what you are talking about but I think that it's pretty balanced. Base version cost 2 exp points which is half a cost of an entire Arcanum level, 4th dot option equals one dot of Life. For that you get some useless cat hearing, claws and a shape of the tiger - all the thing that you can already do or have very narrow application. But it helps to build Animagus and personalize the character in an iconic way. Imbued Shapechanging also cost 4 dots and doesn't require Life 1 to use it. I might add some progressive drawback to it that makes changing into 'not chosen' animals more difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T18:54:36-07:00","id":1093940,"title":"","content":"It would be simpler to have your character take an Imbued Item or Artifact and it wouldn't go to places the game didn't intend. At any point you could go to an entity to give you an Investment to shape change. Basically, there are ways to get what the character wants without doing something bogus to the arcana practices and it would be more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T23:34:25-07:00","id":1094008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1093940#post1093940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be simpler to have your character take an Imbued Item or Artifact and it wouldn't go to places the game didn't intend. At any point you could go to an entity to give you an Investment to shape change. Basically, there are ways to get what the character wants without doing something bogus to the arcana practices and it would be more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Practices work as they were, I don't see what changed. You just get access to them a little earlier for a very, very specific, mostly useless set of spells. It lets you play Sirius Black without having to be almost a master of arcanum. If its more interesting for you to have it from an entity you can always reskin the merit, It's just a homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T00:19:57-07:00","id":1094021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1094008#post1094008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It lets you play Sirius Black without having to be almost a master of arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sirius Black was one of a handful of people who did the strenuous practice necessary to become an Animagus off the record in his setting. I would not represent his ability with a Merit whose only prerequisites are basic knowledge of the Life Arcanum and minimally above-average Stamina.<br /> <br /> Your Merit lets you play Sirius Black with more granular control of his transformation and none of the massive effort Sirius Black put into learning the trick you're emulating, which makes him a poor fit as an example of what you're purporting the Merit is for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T00:32:19-07:00","id":1094023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1094021#post1094021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sirius Black was one of a handful of people who did the strenuous practice necessary to become an Animagus off the record in his setting. I would not represent his ability with a Merit whose only prerequisites are basic knowledge of the Life Arcanum and minimally above-average Stamina.<br /> <br /> Your Merit lets you play Sirius Black with more granular control of his transformation and none of the massive effort Sirius Black put into learning the trick you're emulating, which makes him a poor fit as an example of what you're purporting the Merit is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be right about his effort but it was something that he was born with, not everyone can be an animagus. And 4 dots or merit <i>is</i> a lot of effort. Just compare it with 4 dots of Resources, Proffesional Training or Status.<br /> Edit: 3 dots of stamina is above average, not minimaly above average. 4 dots represent a beast who runs and sometimes wins the marathon. That said, If you wish to use the merit you bump the prerequisits to numbers you think are more correct.<br /> Edit 2: Real prerequisit of a full change is 3 dots of Life with base merit and 2 with full option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 05-18-2017, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T00:55:26-07:00","id":1094032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1094008#post1094008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Practices work as they were, I don't see what changed. You just get access to them a little earlier for a very, very specific, mostly useless set of spells. It lets you play Sirius Black without having to be almost a master of arcanum. If its more interesting for you to have it from an entity you can always reskin the merit, It's just a homebrew.</div> </div> </div> </div>It skews the scale at which Practices are accessed, even if it is in only a limited way it essentially unlocks superior powers for a Life Mage. Also, it isn't mostly useless, even if you're only limited to one animal to shift into then there are -lots- of good options to choose from that could accomplish very unique tasks. Seriously, just use an Imbued Item, it costs the same and you're not stuck being just one kind of animal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T01:08:06-07:00","id":1094036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1094032#post1094032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It skews the scale at which Practices are accessed, even if it is in only a limited way it essentially unlocks superior powers for a Life Mage. Also, it isn't mostly useless, even if you're only limited to one animal to shift into then there are -lots- of good options to choose from that could accomplish very unique tasks. Seriously, just use an Imbued Item, it costs the same and you're not stuck being just one kind of animal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should unlock superior powers, it's a merit afterall. But with a cost of half a dot of Arcanum... I would think for a long moment if I really need it. But it's a cool Mystery that gives player what he would like to play and doesn't step up a game by giving him power over aggr damage. <br /> I understand your point. It's a homebrew though so under every one merit here there is written &quot;Use under ST approval.&quot;<br /> <br /> Imbued Item has a fixed effect so it might not be possible to choose a form you want to change into. I'm not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T01:28:02-07:00","id":1094039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1094036#post1094036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imbued Item has a fixed effect so it might not be possible to choose a form you want to change into. I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you create it OOC you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T01:32:22-07:00","id":1094041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1094039#post1094039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you create it OOC you can.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that you can do it only once(as a ST introducing it into play or as player when creating a character) and after that it works only in that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T01:36:38-07:00","id":1094044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1094041#post1094041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean that you can do it only once(as a ST introducing it into play or as player when creating a character) and after that it works only in that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on how you read it when it says that it stores a spell. I'd certainly allow an item Imbued with Shapechanging to change you into more than one form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T01:46:44-07:00","id":1094047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1094044#post1094044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That depends on how you read it when it says that it stores a spell. I'd certainly allow an item Imbued with Shapechanging to change you into more than one form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea. That was my interpretation also but I had a game with a player who took 9 dots worth of Artifact merit that holded almost entire 5th dot of Forces(Create and Eradicate Energy). It's a lot of exp and the player was a gentlemen that didn't abuse it but it made me think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T09:17:30-07:00","id":1094173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1094047#post1094047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea. That was my interpretation also but I had a game with a player who took 9 dots worth of Artifact merit that holded almost entire 5th dot of Forces(Create and Eradicate Energy). It's a lot of exp and the player was a gentlemen that didn't abuse it but it made me think.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what they're there for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T02:47:02-07:00","id":1101900,"title":"","content":"<b>Divergent Blessing (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Proximus<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The power in your blood manifests differently than most of your kin. You can add a Blessing in one of your Dynasty's Arcana, with a dot rating equal to the dots in this merit, to your list of available Blessings.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> This replaces a number of dots of Blessings equal to the dots in this merit - you are effectively swapping some spells for another one. Sanctity of Merits still applies if you are swapping out Blessings you already possess.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: This gives a little bit more flexibility as far as spells go with existing Proximus Dynasties. If there is one Proximus Dynasty you mostly like, but just wish it had a few spells different, now you can adjust it.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:18:48-07:00","id":1107069,"title":"","content":"<b>Merit: Adamant Blade (</b>\u25cf\u25cf)<br /> Prerequisite: Adamant Hand \u25cf\u25cf, Adamantine Arrow Status \u25cf<br /> Effect: You have studied the advanced principles of the Adamant Way, further melding your magical skills with your martial arts. When you cast a damaging spell, you may choose to focus its Imago through the lens of your martial training, resulting in the following effects:<ul><li>The spell manifests in the approximate shape of a melee weapon of your choice. This effect is obviously supernatural and reflects the Arcanum used - Death creates a dagger of writhing shadow, Forces generates a spear of crackling lightning, Matter collects shards of masonry and earth from the environment and forms makeshift brass knuckles, etc.</li> <li>These &quot;spell-weapons&quot; do not have weapon modifiers or apply Initiative penalties, but you may make All-Out Attacks, attempt called shots, and apply the effects of any applicable Fighting Styles you know. (This includes the use of Brawl-based styles if you create a brass-knuckles equivalent. If you know Two-Weapon Fighting, you conjure a second weapon in your other hand.)</li> <li>Attacking with a spell-weapon uses Strength + Weaponry (substitute Brawl if you conjure brass knuckles or equivalents; substitute Dexterity if you have Fighting Finesse.) Damage is equivalent to the spell's Potency. Do not add successes on your attack roll as additional damage. On an Exceptional Success, regain a point of Willpower and a point of Mana, as your martial skill echoes the Supernal truth of the Adamant Way.</li> <li>The spell automatically gains Advanced Duration, lasting for one scene. You roll for Paradox once, at the time the spell is initially cast. If Sleepers witness your casting, they impact the Paradox roll as normal; if they stumble into the fight mid-scene, their Quiescence slowly degrades your spell-weapon's Potency. If you Reach to deal aggravated damage, you must spend 1 Mana per strike, but you may choose not to pay this cost and deal lethal damage at any time during the spell's duration.</li> <li>If you are disarmed of a spell-weapon, it automatically re-forms or returns to your hands on your next turn. (If the disarming maneuver uses bare hands, the opponent may take damage from touching the spell-weapon at Storyteller discretion.) The spell-weapon may be dispelled or cancelled as normal.</li> <li>If you already know the spell as a rote, you may substitute the combat skill being used (Brawl or Weaponry) for the usual rote skill, and this rote skill receives the +1 Order affinity bonus.</li> <li>Mundane armor applies to spell-weapons on an Arcanum-by-Arcanum basis. Common sense and Storyteller discretion apply; as a general rule, if the same spell could be used to attack an object, then mundane armor applies (but if a single attack deals more damage than the armor's general rating, apply the Pierced Armor tilt.) If the spell could not be used to attack objects, mundane armor does not apply. (Developer's breakdown: Forces, Matter, Prime, Space, Spirit, and Time apply to mundane armor; Death, Life, and Mind bypass it.)</li> <li>Arcanum limitations on targets apply as normal. (E.g. Death blades won't harm constructs that never lived; Life blades won't harm the undead; Mind blades won't harm mindless zombies.)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:19:41-07:00","id":1107070,"title":"","content":"<b>Merit: Adamant Sight (</b>\u25cf<b>)</b><br /> Prerequisite: Adamant Hand \u25cf\u25cf, Adamantine Arrow Status \u25cf<br /> Effect: Active Mage Sight can be an invaluable tool for dealing with magical threats. Without advanced study and practice, however, seeing with the eyes of the Awakened can blind one to mundane dangers. Arrows practiced in the Adamant Way develop pattern-recognition skills that let them filter distractions more effectively, negating the usual -2 penalty to non-magical actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T18:24:34-07:00","id":1107470,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on this one?<br /> <br /> <b>Inherent Magic (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Sleepwalker<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You have some inherent trick of magic as part of your nature. Build out this ability as a Legacy Attainment (Mage: the Awakening 2E pg 198) with a dot rating equal to the dots in this merit. Activating this ability costs at least 1 Willpower - convert any additional Mana costs into additional Willpower that must be spent to use the ability. This ability never provokes Breaking Points for the character to use, though it confers no such immunity to other supernatural events doing so. All major decisions, including Spell Factors, are fixed when this merit is selected.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Such powers are never free. Work with the Storyteller to determine some circumstance that is required to use the ability, or some Condition that it inflicts as a consequence of its use or possession.<br /> <b>Note</b>: This merit may only be selected at character creation or after a significantly transformative event.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: An easy way to give characters a range of flexible supernatural abilities, outside of Supernatural Merits. It's modeled off Legacy Attainments to eliminate much of the Supernal Magic considerations, like Paradox, Dissonance, etc. I might need to add in a line for what to do when you want a conjunctive effect (like &quot;add Arcana X to&quot; expanded effects).]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> would this be a good alternative to Shifter, for when you want a character with an alternate form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-25-2017, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T10:42:44-07:00","id":1108070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1060692#post1060692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was asked how being Mentored by a Supernal Being would look mechanically. Any idea if Mentor / Infamous Mentor merits are good to go with little reskinning, or do they need some bigger tweaks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps something like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/850259-supernal-patron-merit-handshakes-with-god\"><b>this</b></a>?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T21:19:38-07:00","id":1112493,"title":"","content":"<b>Merit: Way of the Shadow's Edge (</b>\u25cf<b>)</b><br /> Prerequisite: Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Adamant Hand \u25cf\u25cf, &quot;Shadow Crafting&quot; rote<br /> Effect: Unique among the Subtle Arcana, Death allows for the manipulation of a Fallen phenomenon - shadows - into tangible shapes, with stolen substance made real enough to sever a limb or deflect a bullet. For Necromancers of all Orders, knowing that a blade or a trusty shield is only a dark corner away has been a source of chill comfort since time immemorial.<br /> <br /> For some Arrows, however, this sort of shadow-crafting is but the first step. Exploiting the fluidity of shadows opens new doors to the seasoned warrior: the shadow in one's hands can shift its shape and size, flickering out like a lash or narrowing to an impossibly-fine point. When wielding weapons born of &quot;Shadow Crafting,&quot; the mage may apply a number of equipment tags (see Hurt Locker, pg. 141) equal to his dots in Death from the following list: Accurate, Bleed, Brawl, Concealed, Grapple, Guard, Knockdown, Piercing, Reach, Stun, Thrown. The mage may change them each turn reflexively; a thrown shadow-blade slithers back to the bearer's hand in the process. Finally, the mage gains additional Reach options for use with the rote:<br /> <br /> +1 Reach, add Matter \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf: The mage imbues the shadows with Matter's solidity, drawing from the other half of the Stygian spectrum. Shadow-crafted weapons, armor, and equipment now have a rating equal to Potency, to a maximum of the mage's Matter dots.<br /> +1 Reach, Death \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf: Shadow-crafted weapons deal aggravated damage at 1 Mana per strike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T02:56:38-07:00","id":1112584,"title":"","content":"Are you aware that you could just use a Death Perfecting spell to increase a shadow's equipment rating, and that Shadow Sculpting would cover weapons that change shape and size and can return to you, and that it's actually desirable to use more than one spell because it increases the chances of a Mage running up against or exceeding his limits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T12:53:36-07:00","id":1112861,"title":"","content":"You got me thinking.<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Mysteries</b>: 3 &amp; 5 dot Merit (Shadow Initiate and Adept)<br /> The merit represents an alignment to the forces of shadow. There needs to be some cause for this to develop, but the character (and possibly player) needn't have any idea what it was.<br /> This connection to shadow manifests as an improved ability to metaphysically connect to shadow. This has a few effects.<ul><li>The character improves their ability to blend into shadows. The drawback is that this applies to penalties, as well.</li> <li><ul><li>At 3 dots, this improves any <i>existing</i> bonus to stealth or concealment from shadows by one. Increase any penalty from excessive lighting by -1.</li> <li>At 5 dots, double any such bonus or penalty from lighting.</li> </ul></li> <li>The character improves their ability to copy or follow someone.<ul><li>At 3 dots, this grants the 9-Again property or 8-Again, if already 9-Again.</li> <li>At 5 dots, this grants 8- and 9-again and the Rote quality to the rolls.</li> <li>The drawback is that the character using this ability cannot exceed the <i>overall</i> success of the person that they are shadowing. If a roll is extended, this limit only applies to the ultimate result, but excessive successes might, if appropriate to the story, provide Conditions.</li> </ul></li> <li>Finally, the connection provides an intimate understanding of the relationship of shadows to the Supernal.<ul><li>\u200bMimicry of another's movements and speech throughout casting and for at least a turn (it cannot be reflexive) qualifies as a Mirror or Shadow Path or Personal Tool Yantra (+1). This can also be used as a Representational Sympathetic Yantra of the subject. (These applications are separate Yantra though they involve only a single physical activity.)</li> <li>\u200bAt 5 dots, all Yantra involving shadow, including mimicry, improve by +1.<br /> Also at 5 dots, the mage can mimic a subject to lock a spell onto their pattern more certainly. This can only be applied to an effect with duration greater than one turn that specifically and directly targets that subject or both that subject and the caster. This grants a +3 (bonus from this merit included) to casting, but the effect's duration ends instantly when the mage ceases copying the subject's physical actions for any reason.\u200b</li> </ul></li> </ul>(At Death 5, a Reach 3 effect can be applied to shadow spells (e.g. <i>Deepen Shadow</i>, or <i>Shadow Sculpting</i>) to grant this Merit for the effect's duration. Some develop it spontaneously and permanently.)<br /> This is overly convoluted, still, I think, but not a bad start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T13:10:45-07:00","id":1112876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1112584#post1112584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you aware that you could just use a Death Perfecting spell to increase a shadow's equipment rating, and that Shadow Sculpting would cover weapons that change shape and size and can return to you, and that it's actually desirable to use more than one spell because it increases the chances of a Mage running up against or exceeding his limits?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Three separate points here; taking them individually.<br /> <br /> RE: use of Perfecting, I'd suggest that there's a good reason why the RAW &quot;Shadow Crafting&quot; just gives the equipment rating as 2 as opposed to Potency: because Matter is the supreme &quot;Hephaestus at his forge&quot; Arcanum, and if you can create &amp; buff items to whatever level you want sans Matter, why take Matter in the first place? To paraphrase this same topic over in the Creative Thaumaturgy thread: stepping on another Arcanum's toes is fine, but making one of its core strengths obsolete isn't. (Put another way: if you want shadows with the strength of titanium, you have to study titanium first.)<br /> <br /> RE: &quot;Shadow Sculpting,&quot; that's another instant action (at best) to cast, plus more instant actions to reshape each turn, which doesn't capture the moment-to-moment reflexive fluidity of martial arts that I was going for.<br /> <br /> RE: &quot;it's actually desirable to use more than one spell because it increases the chances of a Mage running up against or exceeding his limits,&quot; your mileage may vary. Yes, &quot;reach exceeding grasp&quot; and the horrors of unbounded pride are core themes of Mage, but every table is going to differ on how often and how tightly those themes constrain characters' abilities. If you want to say that any capability not already explicitly granted RAW requires a Reach or combined spells, hey, more power to you. Given how tight spell control &amp; combined-spell limits are already, esp. for low-Gnosis mages, I prefer to lean more towards the dark-superhero side of the spectrum and cut them some slack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T14:42:31-07:00","id":1112926,"title":"","content":"Strengthening things is not just the purview of Matter. It is in fact the entire point of Perfecting.<br /> <br /> Shaping shadows with Shadow Sculpting doesn't require any actions after you cast the spell.<br /> <br /> Our opinion differs on the third point, but it's probably irreconcilable so whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T16:07:02-07:00","id":1112980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1112926#post1112926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strengthening things is not just the purview of Matter. It is in fact the entire point of Perfecting.<br /> <br /> Shaping shadows with Shadow Sculpting doesn't require any actions after you cast the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you may have misread me: I'm not disputing what Perfecting is for. My point was that perfecting <i>equipment</i>, your swords-&amp;-shields and other RPG standbys, is Matter's wheelhouse; if you can make a sword <i>without </i>Matter that's better than a sword made <i>with </i>Matter, something's gone awry with Arcana balance. That's why &quot;Platonic Form&quot; imposes a steep Mana-per-swing cost and why &quot;Shadow Crafting,&quot; as written, imposes a hard ceiling on equipment rating - they're both examples of &quot;making equipment without Matter&quot; and are nerfed accordingly.<br /> <br /> RAW, &quot;Shadow Sculpting&quot; doesn't say whether or not continuing to make &amp; remake new shapes requires add'l actions after the spell is cast. My assumption was that it would (and that the shadows would stay where you last put them until the Duration expires, if you stop concentrating and do something else.) Corrective commentary from any devs waiting in the wings is welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T16:34:19-07:00","id":1112984,"title":"","content":"Perfecting equipment bonuses is not part of Matter's purview from what I've read. Who cares that you -might- be able to use Death to create a sword as good as one made with Matter? It likely won't be made of the special material that is the Bane of the spirit you're fighting as it could be if you had used Matter instead. Shadows don't do computation either, so go to Matter if you want to turn your laptop into a super computer. My point is that except in very rare instances (Sympathy mostly) where mechanics were custom made for it, an arcana doesn't have exclusive rights to mechanics.<br /> <br /> Use +1 Reach, animate the shadows, now they do change by themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T13:53:18-07:00","id":1113359,"title":"","content":"Perfecting is <i>not</i> strengthening any phenomenon that is covered by an arcana in any way desired. Rather, it's strengthening it <i>within that purview</i>, which is why Death can make wounds worse by Perfecting, and so forth. The entire argument hinges on what a perfect shadow is and can be, according to the supernal laws. (read as &quot;storyteller fiat&quot;, since there is very little on the topic in the book.)<br /> <br /> Giving material substance to shadows via Death is already a major stretch, so I am quite sympathetic to making further improvements along material lines a reach option with a matter prerequisite.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T16:20:17-07:00","id":1113442,"title":"","content":"That's fine, but it's basically just an argument along lines of opinion at this point, and I disagree with you. Settled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T13:00:28-07:00","id":1128931,"title":"","content":"<b>Sanctum Bindings</b><b>(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: </b>Sanctum \u2022\u2022+<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Through sacred geomancy, you have learned to provide stability to released spells in your Sanctum.<br /> <br /> Benefit: For each dot, one released spell is stable and doesn't risk paradox for its duration as long as its direct effects do not leave the area of the Sanctum. Once leaving though, the countdown begins and will not stop, even if the spell's effects once again are limited to only the Sanctum. Generally, this is used with imbued items to have less worry about their effects going awry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:01:09-07:00","id":1129302,"title":"","content":"<b>Somatic Gestures (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Proximus, Mystic Tools 1+<br /> <b>Effect</b>: You can incorporate the gestures and mudras common to Rotes to bolster your Blessings. Pick one Skill for each Blessing you possess or gain - you can use that Skill as a Yantra for casting that Blessing.<br /> <b>Note: </b>The Storyteller must approve the Skill chosen for the Blessing. and is encouraged to keep to the suggested Rote Skills for that spell. Some thematic deviation is allowed, but having the same Skill for all of the Blessings is frowned upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-24-2017, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T05:19:24-07:00","id":1137984,"title":"","content":"Alright, so I had an idea for a merit to give Proximi a bit of extra free reach with their blessings, and looking back through here it's kinda similar to Vent0's &quot;[Arcana] Prodigy&quot; stuff but at the same time it's a bit more limited and streamlined and goes in a different direction so, just see what you think:<br /> <br /> Enlightened Understanding (\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022, or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Proximus, Occult \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> The proximus understands the fundamental principles behind her blessings a little better than most, and can use that understanding to use said blessings to greater effect without risking paradox.<br /> <br /> With one dot, instead of a single free reach when using a blessing, the proximus instead receives the number that a mage who was capable of casting all of the blessings she knows (and had no more skill in the arcarna than was required to do that) would, in the same manner as an artifact.<br /> In other words, a proximus who knew a one, two and three dot blessing based on spells from the life arcarnum would receive three free reach for the one-dot blessing, two for the two dot blessing, and remain at one free reach for the three dot blessing.<br /> <br /> With three dots in this merit she receives an extra reach on top of this for all blessings. With five dots, two extra reaches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T05:53:30-07:00","id":1137994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1137984#post1137984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so I had an idea for a merit to give Proximi a bit of extra free reach with their blessings, and looking back through here it's kinda similar to Vent0's &quot;[Arcana] Prodigy&quot; stuff but at the same time it's a bit more limited and streamlined and goes in a different direction so, just see what you think:<br /> <br /> Enlightened Understanding (\u2022, \u2022\u2022\u2022, or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Prerequisites: Proximus, Occult \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> The proximus understands the fundamental principles behind her blessings a little better than most, and can use that understanding to use said blessings to greater effect without risking paradox.<br /> <br /> With one dot, instead of a single free reach when using a blessing, the proximus instead receives the number that a mage who was capable of casting all of the blessings she knows (and had no more skill in the arcarna than was required to do that) would, in the same manner as an artifact.<br /> In other words, a proximus who knew a one, two and three dot blessing based on spells from the life arcarnum would receive three free reach for the one-dot blessing, two for the two dot blessing, and remain at one free reach for the three dot blessing.<br /> <br /> With three dots in this merit she receives an extra reach on top of this for all blessings. With five dots, two extra reaches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, though the initial effect is a bit convoluted and favors Dynasties with 3 dot Blessings over those with 1 or 2. Would a 1-3 or 5 Merit tied to single Blessings or Arcana work, you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T06:44:49-07:00","id":1138006,"title":"","content":"I guess. I made it 1-3-5 because after the first dot the bonus applies to everything indiscriminately. If I were to separate it by arcarnum I'd probably make the levels cost 1, 2, and 3. Maybe let it hit 4 or 5 for dynasties without 3 or 2 dot blessings. <br /> <br /> Basically the ideas were &quot;Proximi derive understanding from the blessings they learn&quot;, &quot;make it usable to 3-dot effects&quot; and &quot;don't let them out-reach a full mage&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T07:15:28-07:00","id":1138013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1138006#post1138006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess. I made it 1-3-5 because after the first dot the bonus applies to everything indiscriminately. If I were to separate it by arcarnum I'd probably make the levels cost 1, 2, and 3. Maybe let it hit 4 or 5 for dynasties without 3 or 2 dot blessings. <br /> <br /> Basically the ideas were &amp;quot;Proximi derive understanding from the blessings they learn&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;make it usable to 3-dot effects&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;don't let them out-reach a full mage&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>A version akin to my Rote Mastery Merit could work as well. In this case, it'd grant extra Reach as opposed to adding benefits for using a rote spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T11:23:50-07:00","id":1142234,"title":"","content":"<b>Merit: Way of the Platonic Forge (\u25cf)</b><br /> Prerequisite: Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Adamant Hand \u25cf\u25cf, &quot;Platonic Form&quot; rote<br /> Effect: An Arrow is never defined solely by weapons, but they\u2019re usually handy to have when exploring the world\u2019s dark places. Being able to forge a blade or shield on the anvil of your own will is a neat trick, but Mana resists being trapped in mundane constructs for any length of time. Platonic Form\u2019s steep cost will quickly empty the reserves of any mage in an extended fight. An inventive Obrimos, keen on traveling light, devised this technique to compensate.<br /> <br /> If you Reach to cast Platonic Form with Advanced Duration, each use of the construct as a tool or weapon no longer costs 1 Mana from its supply. The construct\u2019s maximum equipment bonus cannot exceed the mage\u2019s Prime dots, and the spell cannot last longer than one scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T14:28:45-08:00","id":1187647,"title":"","content":"[Thread stumbles out of a Time Iris]<br /> <br /> So, I had the idea for a Merit (or possibly even micro-template) based upon a Sleeper that switches to Sleepwalker (or even Sleepwalker+, with some Spells) when exposed to Magic. But that wears off and they go back to Sleep (only for the cycle to continue the next time conditions are met). <hr /><br /> This is basically me just spit-balling ideas for now - no expectation of it being done or serious is implied.<br /> <br /> <b>Insomagus (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleeper<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your grasp of the Supernal ebbs and flows, leaving you drifting in and out of the Lie. Whenever you are exposed to powerful magic use (such as someone gaining an Exceptional Success on a spell casting roll or triggering Dissonance on an effect that has Withstand beyond dots in this merit), you absorb some of that magic and partially &quot;wake up&quot;, gaining the Awoken Condition. When you have the Awoken Condition, you gain access to a number of Arcana dots equal to the dots in this merit as determined by the circumstances of your temporary Awakening. You are considered to have them all as Ruling Arcana, and can spend Willpower in place of Mana.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> This confers no protection against the actual Breaking Point that triggers activation. Additionally, once the Awoken Condition Lapses, it is usually replaced by another Condition such as Amnesia (regarding the Awoken time), Addicted (regarding experiencing it again), or Frightened (of repeat circumstances).<br /> <br /> -Condition-<br /> <b>Awoken</b><br /> You've seen passed the Lie and become aware to the deeper Truths of the world. While this will fade given time or exposure to Paradox, you can grasp the nature of the world like the Wise do. You gain Peripheral and Active Mage Sight, temporarily swap Integrity for Wisdom, and have an effective Gnosis of 1.<br /> <b>Possible Sources</b>: The Insomagus merit triggering, Breaking Points due witnessing Supernal Magic, Powerful Prime spells.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: After a number of days equal to your current Wisdom (it can resolve immediately if Wisdom drops below this timespan).<br /> <b>Special</b>: Paradox Potency can reduce the number of days before the Condition resolves on a 1-for-1 basis.<br /> <br /> [<u>Comments</u>: I'm thinking of the &quot;trigger&quot; might also absorb the magic (ES spell fails instead, persistent magic ends immediately) to fuel the effect. Also thinking of exact mechanics - Arcana dots seems a bit variable, though flexible in effect. I'm thinking it also needs a more drastic downside, though the Breaking Points incurred, and limited duration impede the &quot;utility&quot; of it. Also, not sure how balanced things are between the Condition and the Merit.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-02-2018, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T08:41:02-08:00","id":1187860,"title":"","content":"Other ideas:<br /> <br /> Would a &quot;line&quot; of Merits based on the Arcana (kind of like Attainments, but not tied to any particular dot rating, nor necessarily requiring that Arcana for its affects)? Scaled for Proximi (who can only pick up their Dynastic Arcana ones), or even Sleepwalkers (giving them vague Arcana leanings)? Something with the same &quot;weight&quot; and &quot;pluggability&quot; as Wolf-Blooded Tells, but for Mage.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ooo. An additional idea, but in the same vein, would be Arcana based Style merits for Sleepwalkers to create Diet-Mages.<br /> <br /> EDIT 2: Which, come to think of it, resembles how Witch Finders did its Mysteries...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-23-2018, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T11:09:47-08:00","id":1190724,"title":"","content":"(Triple posting, ugh. But no one has replied, this is new, and I don't want to complicate Quoting and Liking by having a giant post with different ideas/topics...)<br /> <br /> Stub for another Sleepwalker (mostly) Merit:<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Inspiration (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Non-Mage<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You can gain understanding from the mystic truth that has been entrusted to you and leverage it to empower your own abilities. Whenever you are holding a Spell for a Mage, you gain this merit's dots in a bonus to uses of your own Supernatural merits and abilities that are thematically similar to the Arcana in the spell.<br /> <br /> [<u>Comments</u>: The idea is - holding a spell gives you a bit of a boost, encouraging such behavior. It is limited to Supernatural powers, so it isn't a general bonus, and it needs to be &quot;thematic&quot; to the spells/magics' Arcana. So holding a Forces spell can boost you Pyrokinesis, but not Omen Sensitivity. Thoughts, though?] <hr /><br /> This one is really more intended for Proximi, since their own inherent spell casting limitations reduce the benefit from &quot;free spell control&quot; to &quot;I actually <i>have</i> spell control now&quot;. Still, the other restrictions may limit it enough for general Mages, and there isn't any <i>particular</i> reason why they wouldn't be able to do the same. Depending on how flexible the Storyteller wants to make it, they could either have the &quot;bonus&quot; Spell Control used first (so Gnosis derived Spell Control remains free) or added on &quot;after&quot; Gnosis (which means you'd have to end <i>all</i> &quot;bonus&quot; spells before you can cast on other targets without Reaching).<br /> <br /> <b>Body As Sanctum (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Proximi or Mage<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Some people say they consider their body as a temple - for you, it is a bit more literal. You can treat your body as a Sanctum, increasing allowable Spell Control as long as the spells are limited to your person, up to the lower of you current Stamina or the dots in this merit.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> If your body is a temple, violating it or making it unclean renders the benefits null and void. You lose the benefits of this merit for 24 hours if you Scour your Pattern, gain a Paradox Condition, or (for Proximus) trigger the Severe form of your Curse.<br /> <br /> Here's more of a plot hook, but based on a merit. It could have wider uses, as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Astral Voyeur (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Whenever you connect deeply with someone (such as by helping them fulfill an Aspiration, or satisfy their Virtue or Vice), the next time you sleep, you automatically enter that character's Oneiros.<br /> <br /> <b>Astral Stalker (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Astral Voyeur<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You can return to the souls of those you have connected to previously with Astral Voyeur. By sleeping or meditating, you can enter their Oneiros instead of your own as per the systems for entering the Astral.<br /> <br /> <b>Personal Oblation</b><b> (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The Sleepwalker's soul forms a connection to the Supernal, even if they can't perceive it. They may perform a special ritual (chosen at the time this merit is selected) once a day to generate a single point of Mana. Unless they possess some other way to store it, the Mana condenses into Tass (such as special liquids if the ritual involves brewing, or enchanted bars or coins if it involves smelting, etc.). The Sleepwalker cannot generate more Mana if they are already near 3 or more points worth in Tass form, though they can store excess amounts elsewhere.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: Sleepwalkers as Mana factories. More useful for powering other Mana-based abilities if they don't have access to Mages or Hallows, and as a spring-board to other Merits - such as a generalized Imbued Item merit for Awakened-lite Mad Scientists. The variable ritual nature can evoke witches brewing Tass potions, Enlightened Scientist conducting experiments to charge Tass batteries, and more besides.]<br /> <br /> <b>Mystic Panoply (\u2022\u2022\u2022+, Special)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have magic inherent to you that manifests in your belongings, as opposed to what you can wield directly. Treat this merit as a special version of Enhanced Item, except the magic is tied more to you, and you can modify which object(s) is/are affected and the spell effects by conducting a 3 hour long ritual (specific to the character) and spending a point of Willpower.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: This gives a little specific magic to a character, without the considerations of full spell-casting. Because it is limited to Enhanced Item - persistent, rather than activated effects - this reduces the potential cheese the owner can get up to.] <hr /><br /> <br /> Also, is it me, or do a number of the Merits in the Mage-only section seem like they would make decent stand-alone Supernatural merits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-01-2018, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T09:15:39-07:00","id":1201293,"title":"","content":"How well would reskinning the Favored Form Merit from Werewolf work in Mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T09:19:34-07:00","id":1201294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1201293#post1201293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How well would reskinning the Favored Form Merit from Werewolf work in Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the mage only has one form the benefits would be much more potent than for werewolves who shifts between forms with or without the benefits (and the human form specifically can't gain the benefits), and the drawback wouldn't work at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-30-2018, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T22:23:10-07:00","id":1201855,"title":"","content":"How about...<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Optimized Form (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Prerequisites</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Life 3 \u201cMany Faces\u201d as a Praxis, Gnosis at Merit rating +1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Effect</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: The shapeshifting mage favors one shape among many, and has learned to optimize it. Design and choose a single form the mage can change into via the \u201cMany Faces\u201d spell. With each dot in this Merit, he gains a specific advantage when in that form. Attribute increases from this Merit apply to derived traits.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u2022: Choose a Physical Skill. The mage achieves exceptional success at three successes when using that Skill.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u2022\u2022: Choose a Physical Attribute. The mage gains an extra dot of that Attribute.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022: Choose a Praxis other than &quot;Many Faces&quot; that uses the Life Arcanum. Upon its exceptional success, the mage can choose two benefits instead of one.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: Choose another Physical Attribute to raise as per the second-dot effect.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: Choose a relevant Skill. The mage gains the advanced action quality when using that Skill.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Drawback</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Optimizing one form among many comes at the cost of others. When in her natural form, the mage's total Attribute dots are reduced by the half the Merit's rating, rounded up, divided among Attributes. Furthermore, shapeshifting to any form other than the optimized form requires a Reach.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Note</b>: This Merit can only be chosen for one form that can be assumed by Many Faces, up to minute details. Missing even a single detail means the mage cannot benefit from the Merit.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T08:10:35-07:00","id":1209630,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Language (The Parametric Language) (\u2022)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Prerequisites</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: High Speech</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Effect</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: The mage knows of the Parametric Language, the secret tongue of the Gate, which His followers claim She used to open and then banish the Abyss. When casting spells targeting Abyssal entities and phenomena, the mage may use the Parametric Language instead of High Speech as mantras and runes for purpose of Yantras. Doing so grants a +3 bonus instead of the usual +2, but adds a +1 to the spell's Paradox dice pool.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Parametric Language can be used in conversation, albeit clumsily and slowly. When spoken to Abyssal entities, however, it improves the mage's impression by one step in Social Maneuvering. Often, this is the minimum required to have a meaningful social interaction with an Abyssal entity at all.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T03:43:57-07:00","id":1212988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1063177#post1063177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll get back to Hammer ( I edited the previous post) but in the meanwhile...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Practice Mastery</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Style)</span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gnosis 3, Access to a Practice</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Effect:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You have devoted yourself to a single Practice. Merit doesn\u2019t work with Rotes since they have no place for your artistry. Praxis are compatible. Can be taken multiple times, each for a different practice.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Specialty</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022) -- Choose a Specialty in a Practice. When using it you benefit from usual +1 dice. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>So Below</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022) -- The mage can stabilize a spell by putting a chunk of the Supernal Realms strength. Spend 1 Mana to grant Advanced Potency.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Deeper Studies</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022\u2022) -- Deep understanding of a Practice allows him to always be aware of changes he can make in the surrounding world. It allows him to cast a spell reflexively at the cost of 1 Reach. He can\u2019t use Yantras that are not reflexive when doing so. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Mastery</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) -- Mage achieves full proficiency in spinning his spells. When it encounters the will of others Mage gets +1 to CoW</span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>love it, but isn't the reflexive casting too strong?<br /> maybe a bonus yantra slot when casting from that Practice, instead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1djeav1YTEwQq1fkDtWEKh7PPVFmzj3y-\" target=\"_blank\">The Repository</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13158-sir-bardiel","name":"Sir Bardiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13158_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:52:14-07:00","id":1213077,"title":"","content":"I agree that reflexive casting is really strong. If such a thing would be possible to gain through Merits I'd personally limit it to a single Rote or Praxis per Merit.<br /> <br /> Specialty: Rather than mixing rules for different traits, why not just grant a +1 bonus to all spells using the Practice? One die equals half a step of a spell factor. I think that's balanced since you can't retake the Merit for the same Practice.<br /> <br /> So Below &amp; Mastery: I don't think stacking them would be unbalanced since you can get Advanced Potency regardless, but it's a bit boring having similar benefits like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> I also have two suggestion your Style. The dot rating is just where I'd put them if I had a 1-5 dot Style. You're of course free to move them around if you use them.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Nature (should have a better name) (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Spells cast using the chosen Practice seems to weigh less. If the mage has at least one active spell of the chosen Practice, she may ignore one of them for the purpose of Spell Control.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> This only affects one spell, even if the mage holds multiple versions of this Merit for different Practices. It also does not affect spells being cast. If a mage who already holds a number of active spells equal to their Gnosis casts one spell using the chosen Practice, that spell still requires one additional Reach to cast even if it would not count towards spell control.<br /> <br /> <b>Practical Insight (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> Through intense studies of this Practice the mage can cast spells using deeper levels of understanding than thought possible. When casting non-Rote spells using the chosen Practice, count the mage's Gnosis as two dots higher for purposes of ritual intervals, and increase both the maximum number of Yantras and Paradox dice incurred for each Reach above Arcanum limits by one. If the character is already at Gnosis 9 or 10, simply half the ritual interval to 30 seconds (10 turns).<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Once gained this Merit applies to all non-Rote spells cast using this Practice. That means even if the mage doesn't cast spells using the improved ritual intervals or maximum number of Yantras, he is still subject to the additional Paradox die should he exceed his maximum number of safe Reaches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T11:17:10-07:00","id":1213126,"title":"","content":"<b>Spell Integrity (\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> When you Relinquish a spell unsafely, you can also infuse it with Mana to fortify it against Paradox. For each point of Mana you spend (up to your per turn limit), the spell will ignore one interval check for Paradox on the spell.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: This really just extends the rope you are hanging yourself by with unsafely Relinquishing spells. Still, if you have a surplus of Mana, and need to prepare for a big event, it can mitigate your reckless actions somewhat.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-29-2018, 08:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T13:37:44-07:00","id":1213171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1213126#post1213126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Spell Integrity (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> When you Relinquish a spell unsafely, you can also infuse it with Mana to fortify it against Paradox and Dissonance. For each point of Mana you spend (up to your per turn limit), the spell will ignore one interval check for Paradox or roll to determine the effect of Dissonance on the spell.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: This really just extends the rope you are hanging yourself by with unsafely Relinquishing spells. Still, if you have a surplus of Mana, and need to prepare for a big event, it can mitigate your reckless actions somewhat.]</div> </div> </div> </div>What does the dot rating do? Also, why would it be more possible to defend an unsafely relinquished spell against Dissonance than a safely relinquished or even unrelinquished spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T15:23:22-07:00","id":1213199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1213171#post1213171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What does the dot rating do? Also, why would it be more possible to defend an unsafely relinquished spell against Dissonance than a safely relinquished or even unrelinquished spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I originally intended to have the dot rating have some sort of scaling effect. But I forgot what that was (maybe Mana that could be spent on it?). As for defending against Dissonance, I threw that in there to extend the utility and because Dissonance triggers spell degradation just like normal Unsafe Relinquishment time intervals do. It's more about allowing for unsafe spells to persist a bit longer. I suppose maybe I could extend its Dissonance effects to any spell, it is just a bit better/more useful for Unsafely Relinquished spells?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T15:39:36-07:00","id":1213205,"title":"","content":"I think you should remove the effect on Dissonance entirely since Dissonance affects all spells equally; not just unsafely relinquished spells. Extending the effect to all spells would instead make the Merit less focused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T09:06:33-07:00","id":1213451,"title":"","content":"I've updated one that I really liked from the Mage Chronicler's Guide that I think is in the same mould as other Merits in this thread that give a character increased access to Reach while also emphasizing the benefits of certain kinds of Yantras.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessed Sacrament (</b><b>\u2022 </b><b>to </b><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) </b>- Note: Based on &quot;Magical Components&quot;<br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Awakened<br /> <b>Effect: </b>A basic fact known to all magical traditions around the world is that sacrifice brings power. For each dot in this Merit, you may use a Sacrament Yantra to activate a non-Spell Factors Reach effect in a spell you are casting. The amount of Reach granted is equal to the value of the Yantra.<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Each use of this Merit counts as a separate Yantra, up to your Gnosis-based limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 04-30-2018, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T09:22:24-07:00","id":1213458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1213451#post1213451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've updated one that I really liked from the Mage Chronicler's Guide that I think is in the same mould as other Merits in this thread that give a character increased access to Reach while also emphasizing the benefits of certain kinds of Yantras.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessed Sacrament (</b><b>\u2022 </b><b>to </b><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) </b>- Note: Based on &amp;quot;Magical Components&amp;quot;<br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Awakened<br /> <b>Effect: </b>A basic fact known to all magical traditions around the world is that sacrifice brings power. For each dot in this Merit, you may use a Sacrament Yantra to activate a non-Spell Factors Reach effect in a spell you are casting.<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Each use of this Merit counts as a separate Yantra, up to your Gnosis-based limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this idea, and the drawback definitely balances it out. So, does that mean you need to have two or three dots of this Merit to apply it for Reach Effects that require 2+ Reach? And what if the Sacrament is used to cover one point? The Mage has to use his Reach to fill what's left?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T09:29:52-07:00","id":1213460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1213458#post1213458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like this idea, and the drawback definitely balances it out. So, does that mean you need to have two or three dots of this Merit to apply it for Reach Effects that require 2+ Reach? And what if the Sacrament is used to cover one point? The Mage has to use his Reach to fill what's left?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an excellent point. I've just modified the post so that the Merit specifies that a given Sacrament Yantra grants as many Reach as its Yantra bonus, namely to a maximum of +3. This <i>may </i>be a little overpowered, but given that +3 Yantras are very rare and require items taken from various Invisible Realms, I think it balances out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-04T07:15:46-07:00","id":1224675,"title":"","content":"So, I was thinking of something similar to Herald (aka Imbued Person), but for Enhanced Item. Basically, Sleepwalker-with-permanent-spells-applied represented mechanically, and possibly with a little twist/extra. Since this would be intended for a &quot;standalone&quot; Sleepwalker (focus character is the Enhanced Sleepwalker, not the source applying the spells), so of the variations I was thinking of were <b>A)</b> the effect were suppressible but not dispellable or <b>B)</b> Spells cast upon the subject (up to X) just naturally last longer without needing Reach (making it <i>really easy</i> to Enhance them with Indefinite spells) or <b>C)</b> they can modify the spell factors of spell that are &quot;on&quot; them (up to the limits of the Merit dots).<br /> <br /> I was thinking more <b>A</b>, since that makes the spell effects more of an inherent part of the character, that merely uses Enhanced Item and Spells as the mechanical scaffolding.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T04:05:54-07:00","id":1228543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to have a Befouled Praxis or rote, but you don't need any training to Befoul a Praxis when you buy it - just to know that it's possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1077177#post1077177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's an additional threshold (on top of knowing that it's even possible) that stops both players and characters from dabbling with Antinomian magic. Characters can't really be tempted to it in a weak or pressed moment since it requires an amount of effort to even learn how to do it, and I can see players skipping it because of the XP cost (even if they already plan on becoming Nasnasi since by then they wouldn't need befouled Praxes/Rotes anyway). I know it's just one XP to technically become a Rabashakim, but then you'd only have a single spell you're able to befoul. And I'd imagine you've already learned most spells you'd want to befoul as Praxes and Rotes already unless you're a very fresh mage.<br /> <br /> In case anyone else feels the same I can repeat the same suggestion I've already given to my group: Have it be possible for mages to befoul Praxes without having to learn new ones. I do actually like the concept of Antinomian Rotes as separate from regular Rotes since they're specialized Imagos, but Praxes are spells that a mage knows inside and out, and you could make an argument that you wouldn't have to relearn a spell you know by heart in order to befoul it as if it were a spell you were relatively unfamiliar with.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I have two solutions to something I'd like to change (others might not, and that's also okay; this post isn't for you).<br /> <br /> 1.) The suggestion in my own quote. Just make it possible for anyone who knows that it is possible to befoul any of their own Praxes.<br /> <br /> 2.) This following Merit:<br /> <i><b>Antinomian Casting (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></i><br /> Your character can befoul her own spells instead of relying on Antinomian Rotes created by other Scelesti. She can now choose to befoul any of her Praxes when she cast them. As it is part of the Imago, that decision must be made at the same step as deciding Spell Factors.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> This only applies to spells she's intimately connected to. Creative thaumaturgy and non-Antinomian Rotes are still outside your Reach as only a Rabashakim.<br /> <br /> I would use this either in combination with a house rule that disallows learning specifically Antinomian Praxes, or allow any duplicate Praxis (as in, knowing one regular Praxis and its Antinomian counterpart) to be refunded as one Arcane Experience, similar to Legacy Attainments.<br /> How this interacts with Joining remains to be seen when the updated rules for Scelesti are published. Hopefully that's on the way with the recently revealed Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed that's in first drafts right now.<br /> <br /> Edit: For a left-handed campaign where all player characters are supposed to become Scelesti, you could discount the Merit with each Antinomian Rote learned. Antinomian Rotes learned after buying the Merit with apply Sanctity of Merits on any non-discounted dots. Same thing with becoming a Nasnas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-19-2018, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T05:28:09-07:00","id":1228552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1224675#post1224675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was thinking of something similar to Herald (aka Imbued Person), but for Enhanced Item. Basically, Sleepwalker-with-permanent-spells-applied represented mechanically, and possibly with a little twist/extra. Since this would be intended for a &amp;quot;standalone&amp;quot; Sleepwalker (focus character is the Enhanced Sleepwalker, not the source applying the spells), so of the variations I was thinking of were <b>A)</b> the effect were suppressible but not dispellable or <b>B)</b> Spells cast upon the subject (up to X) just naturally last longer without needing Reach (making it <i>really easy</i> to Enhance them with Indefinite spells) or <b>C)</b> they can modify the spell factors of spell that are &amp;quot;on&amp;quot; them (up to the limits of the Merit dots).<br /> <br /> I was thinking more <b>A</b>, since that makes the spell effects more of an inherent part of the character, that merely uses Enhanced Item and Spells as the mechanical scaffolding.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>B sounds like Hollow Ones, so A with a dash of C sounds nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T06:54:50-07:00","id":1228571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1228552#post1228552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> B sounds like Hollow Ones, so A with a dash of C sounds nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking <b>A</b>: For what ever spell(s) they purchase with the Merit, they can perform a kind of &quot;reverse Dissonance&quot; roll - at the end of a Scene, they can roll Integrity to reinforce any Spell Factors that have been degraded (by Dissonance, for example) up to their original settings. I'll probably throw in an additional point that the Duration Factor of the spell cannot be reduced or eliminated, and that ending the spell (such as by a Lasting Dispel Magic or Counterspelling) merely sets all factors to 0.<br /> <br /> <b>C</b>, I'll separate out into a different Merit. Maybe related to Spell Thief, or at least complementary to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T07:45:33-07:00","id":1228581,"title":"","content":"Forgot if I added this before, but here's a mage merit that I've included in my own chronicle:<br /> <br /> Potent Mage Sight: The strength of your vision is greater than those of your peers. You just seem to have that edge on them. Where others barely fail, you barely succeed, grasping at the truth of the supernal.<br /> 3 dot merit, add one die to each revelation and scrutiny roll. This does modify how many rolls you can make before risking bleeding your nimbus into the mystery.<br /> <br /> I felt that 3 dots was appropriate given that the game is about mysteries. Also, it's just cheap enough to possibly be worth not increasing your gnosis or your arcana, but just expensive enough to justify it being universal.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-19T11:22:02-07:00","id":1228630,"title":"","content":"<u>Version 1</u> - Mirrors Enhanced Item exactly. Plays fast and loose with mechanics.<br /> <br /> <b>Enhanced Form (\u2022+, Special)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have absorbed a spell into your Pattern, and made it part of your being. You are the recipient of a number of permanent spells (similar to Enhanced Item, but with the character as the subject instead of an object). Should Dissonance degrade the Spell Factors of these spells, the character can make their own Dissonance roll (Integrity vs a Withstand of the spell's dot level) at the end of each Scene to instead restore Spell Factors to their original level, even from 0. Dissonance cannot reduce the Duration Factor (and is not counted when determining which Spell Factor to reduce next.<br /> <br /> <u>Version 2</u> - Spells out the exact benefits available. Keeps power restrained by merit dots.<br /> <br /> <b>Enhanced Form (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have absorbed a spell into your Pattern, and made it part of your being. You can retain a persistent spell active upon you, with an Arcana rating of no more than the dots in this merit. The spell can only utilize the free Reach available to it as if cast by a Mage with Arcana of this merit's dots (so at 5 dots, a 3 dot spell would have 3 free Reach). Additional Spell Factors' dice penalties can not exceed this merit's dot rating x 2. Should Dissonance degrade the Spell Factors of these spells, the character can make their own Dissonance roll (Integrity vs a Withstand of the spell's dot level) at the end of each Scene to instead restore Spell Factors to their original level, even from 0. Dissonance cannot reduce the Duration Factor (and is not counted when determining which Spell Factor to reduce next.<br /> <b>Special:</b> A character can have multiple versions of this merit, each representing a different persistent spell.<br /> <br /> <b>Enhanced Form, Advanced (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Enhanced Form \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You can add dots in this Merit for calculating the additional Spell Factors for Enhanced Form.<br /> <br /> <u>Special Options</u> - Could apply to either version above.<br /> <sup>1</sup> <b>Special:</b> Should the spell be undone (such as a Lasting Dispel Magic), the character can reacquire the same spell at the end of the Chapter via Sanctity of Merits, even if there is not a Mage available to cast it.<br /> <sup>2</sup> <b>Special:</b> Should the spell be undone (such as a Lasting Dispel Magic), the spell is instead treated as if it had all Spell Factors other than Duration reduced to 0.<br /> <br /> <u>Further Additions</u><br /> For Version 2, I could see one allowing for Combined Arcana.<br /> I can see a followup merit for either (but mostly 2) that lets one spend an action to adjust the Spell Factors within the current range (move them around, but not increase or decrease the dice penalty).<br /> Related to the above, I could also see adding additional Reach effects... at the cost of either temporary instability, Paradox Conditions, or automatically Contained Paradox (so, resistant Damage).<br /> <br /> So, thoughts, preferences? <hr /><br /> Another idea that could use some revision. Maybe obviate some prior merits, so entirely optional.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Adept (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Sleepwalker<br /> <b>Effect:</b> When rolling dice for Supernal magic where Gnosis would be used (such as activating Imbued Items), you can instead use your rating in this Merit.<br /> [<u>Comments</u>: So, this one is very niche and reliant on the amount of interaction a ST is already allowing Sleepwalkers to have with any rolls that involve Gnosis. Imbued items are one example. Allowing <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1083833#post1083833\">Rote Sorcery</a> is another. If they want, it's possible that it could aid Proximus Blessing usage, even though the normal Gnosis + Arcana pool was replaced with Resolve + Composure.] <hr /><br /> Here's another tentative idea.<br /> <br /> <b>See the Threads (\u2022\u2022, Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Empathy 1<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your character can see the threads of connection that bind people and objects together. They can make a Wits + Empathy - Sympathetic Range Withstand to identify the connection something has to something else. They may not know why this cup is important to He-Who-Must-Not-Be-Named (or even who that is), but they can tell it has a strong bond with <i>someone</i> (and even identify that person, should they meet).<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> You can't <i>not</i> see the threads everywhere. You know when two people are faking affection for each other, and figuring out just why that knife is important can get you killed. Additionally, whenever you identify a Sympathetic Connection and have current Willpower less that its Connection Withstand, the party at the other end gets some inkling that you <i>know</i> of their Connection to what you glimpsed.<br /> <br /> <b>Unravelling Touch (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Occult 1<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Something about you unravels the Imago of spells you come across. You obviously aren't a Sleeper, and you don't suffer Quiescence, but magic you come into contact with is undone all the same. Upon touching an active spell effect (or being the subject of one), Reflexively roll a Clash of Wills against it with Resolve + Composure. Upon success, the spell ends or is prevented from affecting you. If the spell's highest Arcana exceeds your Occult Skill, you lose one point of Willpower upon making the roll. You can only unravel one spell effect each turn, but will continue to do so until you either are no longer in contact with a spell, or you run out of Willpower and the spell's rating exceeds your Occult.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> This is an automatic reaction - you don't have a choice or not, even if the spell is beneficial or wanted. Mages also tend to view you as a hazard or tool, complicating your life in other ways.<br /> <br /> <b>Resonating Presence (\u2022\u2022, Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Presence 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have a powerful presence - so much so that you warp nearby Leylines, Loci, and Hallows to match it. This merit is tied to a single Resonance type. Any Leyline, Locus, or Hallow within Presence * 10 yards has their Resonance overwritten with yours. This persists for as long as you remain in the area, reverting immediately once you leave.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> You stick out to occult senses like a signal flare on a dark night. Spirits and other entities disposed toward your Resonance will flock to you. Beings opposed to it will try to drive you off or kill you. Your life will the center of a battle you may not even be able to perceive.<br /> <br /> <b>Fundamental Flux (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Stamina 2<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You have the ability to manipulate the resilience of whatever you touch. Under stress (such as combat, or intense interactions) you can increase or decrease the Durability of whatever material you are in contact with. When you are inhaling, anything touching you has its Durability increased by your Stamina. When you are exhaling, whatever you touch has its Durability reduced by your Stamina.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Since the effect is keyed to stress and your breathing, managing it effectively can be tricky. All it takes is a bad exhalation at the wrong time when excited to cause your bike to collapse under the slightest jolt, or, in rare cases, your clothes to shred in a strong wind. Mediation can help regulate the stress that causes it to happen, but once you lose your cool, only situational awareness and timing will help you.<br /> <br /> Idea for a temporal one - Whenever the character undergoes a Breaking Point, they go backwards and/or forwards in time. They still <i>had</i> the Breaking Point (including from Dissonance?) but might be able to act before the triggering event occurs. Since it keys of Breaking Points, exploiting the mechanic is.. problematic. Or just traumatic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-10-2018, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T20:28:21-07:00","id":1241140,"title":"","content":"No commentary on the above?<br /> <br /> What about a temporal one that has the Sleepwalker seeing a few seconds ahead (basically, a permanent Present as Past)?<br /> <hr /><br /> Here's a minor one for accomplished Artificers:<br /> <br /> <b>Rote Activation (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Imbue Item Attainment, any Rote<br /> <b>Effect:</b> When Imbuing a Rote spell into an item, you can encode the Rote's Skill Yantra into the trigger, allowing other users to add their own ranks in that skill to their activation rolls for the Imbued Item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T18:17:37-07:00","id":1244337,"title":"","content":"Here is an experimental concept:<br /> <br /> <b>Usurp Control (\u2022\u2022, Attainment)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Prime 2, Counterspell<br /> <b>Effect:</b> When you succeed in a Counterspell, you can spend an additional point of Mana to take control of the spell instead of cancelling it. You can determine post-casting decisions, such as specific targets for the spell (but not Spell Factors or Reach options), and you count the spell against your own Spell Control.<br /> <b>Note:</b> The spell's Range is still determined from its original source, which may affect targeting options for spells that were intended to be thrown.<br /> <br /> <s><b>Assum</b>ING DIRECT CONTROL</s><br /> <b>Assume Control (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Attainment)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Prime 4, Usurp Control, Dispel Magic or Supernal Dispellation<br /> <b>Effect:</b> When you suppress an active spell in a Lasting manner (via Dispel Magic and similar effects), you can spend an additional point of Mana to engage in a Clash of Wills for control of the spell instead of cancelling it. Upon success, the spell is counted against your Spell Control, and you can make the same decisions regarding the spell (reducing Spell Factors, cancelling it, Relinquishing it, etc.) as if you had cast it. If the your Clash roll fails, the spell is still cancelled.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, the Merit sub-type above is for covering alternative Arcana Attainments, without necessarily replacing the existing ones. If adapting the existing Attainments using this method, each new rating in a Arcanum would grant a free Attainment Merit rated at the same level. As for these specific ones, it is a method for swapping spells, &quot;refreshing&quot; Relinquished spells (by Counterspelling them, then re-Relinquishing them), and &quot;spell reflection&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-10-2018, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T19:01:24-07:00","id":1244344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1244337#post1244337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is an experimental concept:<br /> <br /> <s><b>Assum</b>ING DIRECT CONTROL</s><br /> <b>Assume Control (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Attainment)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Prime 4, Counterspell<br /> <b>Effect:</b> When you succeed in a Counterspell, you can spend an additional point of Mana to take control of the spell instead of cancelling it. The spell is counted against your Spell Control, and you can make the same decisions regarding the spell (reducing Spell Factors, cancelling it, Relinquishing it, etc.) as if you had cast it. If you succeed in Counterspelling as it is cast, you can choose new targets and make other similar choices for the spell as long as the Reach and Spell Factors remain unchanged.<br /> [<u>Comments:</u> So, the Merit sub-type above is for covering alternative Arcana Attainments, without necessarily replacing the existing ones. If adapting the existing Attainments using this method, each new rating in a Arcanum would grant a free Attainment Merit rated at the same level. As for this specific one, it is a method for swapping spells, &amp;quot;refreshing&amp;quot; Relinquished spells (by Counterspelling them, then re-Relinquishing them), and &amp;quot;spell reflection&amp;quot;.]</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, could relinquished spells be Counterspelled at all? I thought it had to be done while the spell is being cast? Or is this Attainment specifically designed to cover that?<br /> <br /> Anyways, damn I was going to do something similar for Attainments of the Timori and any other Banisher Legacies. * takes notes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T03:18:21-07:00","id":1244433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1244344#post1244344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, could relinquished spells be Counterspelled at all? I thought it had to be done while the spell is being cast? Or is this Attainment specifically designed to cover that?<br /> <br /> Anyways, damn I was going to do something similar for Attainments of the Timori and any other Banisher Legacies. * takes notes</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterspell is generally a &quot;remove magic with a Clash if Wills&quot; effect. Using it to &quot;block&quot; a spell actually requires the Mage to have Active Mage Sight up - otherwise they can't.<br /> <br /> Relinquished spells are still spells, just ones which aren't actively monitored or sustained. They can be CoW'd/Counterspelled normally.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I've been reading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-10-2018, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T03:32:09-07:00","id":1244436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1244433#post1244433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Counterspell is generally a &amp;quot;remove magic with a Clash if Wills&amp;quot; effect. Using it to &amp;quot;block&amp;quot; a spell actually requires the Mage to have Active Mage Sight up - otherwise they can't.<br /> <br /> Relinquished spells are still spells, just ones which aren't actively monitored or sustained. They can be CoW'd/Counterspelled normally.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I've been reading it.</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought AMS was needed to perceive the spell\u2019s Imago as it was being formed, after which you\u2019d need Dispel Magic or Supernal Dispellation to suppress/remove spells. <br /> <br /> But even so, an Attainment that bypasses such restrictions sound plausible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T04:32:29-07:00","id":1244445,"title":"","content":"21C Hermit is right. Counterspell requires AMS to perceive the Imago so that you can disrupt the Imago before the spell comes into existence. It does nothing to spells that have already been cast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T09:21:28-07:00","id":1244521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1244445#post1244445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">21C Hermit is right. Counterspell requires AMS to perceive the Imago so that you can disrupt the Imago before the spell comes into existence. It does nothing to spells that have already been cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I was reading the last line as a &quot;to use this Attainment to counter a spell before it is cast&quot; not &quot;to use this Attainment <i>at all</i>&quot;. I'll modify the above merit.<br /> <br /> I broke the two effects into separate Merits/Attainments, with the &quot;take control of pre-existing spell&quot; one dependent upon the previous one, and tied into Dispel Magic and similar effects (but only if Lasting - any lesser duration runs the risk of you just deciding to Cancel it before your control expires, which removes much of the incentive for the Lasting Reach option).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-10-2018, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T09:49:49-07:00","id":1244530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1244344#post1244344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, could relinquished spells be Counterspelled at all? I thought it had to be done while the spell is being cast? Or is this Attainment specifically designed to cover that?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you were right - Counterspell itself is only as the spell is being cast. I broke up the functionality into two Merit/Attainments, edited above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1244344#post1244344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, damn I was going to do something similar for Attainments of the Timori and any other Banisher Legacies. * takes notes</div> </div> </div> </div>It also occurred to me that Counterspelling takes an Instant Action. There may be some room for something that make it (Usurp Control optional) Reflexive, so long as you are in contact with the target or source - a kind of &quot;spell-drinking-grip&quot;. Another option is for a &quot;curse&quot; like effect that sticks to a target and rewrites all their spells' Target to &quot;the caster&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-07T10:14:04-07:00","id":1252259,"title":"","content":"<b>Flesh of Shadows (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Stamina 2+, Resolve 2+<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Something in your very substance calls to the darkness, yearning to join it. Unless bathed in bright light (such as outdoors during daylight, or in full illumination indoors), you can merge with the shadows for Stamina + Resolve in Turns by spending a point of Willpower. While a shadow, you are two-dimensional, have no mass or substance, and can move through cracks and crevices, but you are still affected by gravity and cannot interact with physical objects.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Inside complete darkness, your body becomes shadows without your choice. Sleeping with the light on may become an obsession to avoid the disquieting feeling of being bodiless for long periods of time.<br /> <br /> <b>Reaper's Touch (\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Resolve 3+<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Your touch steals vitality from the vulnerable, leeching them to feed you... whether you want to or not. Whenever you touch someone with Lethal or Aggravated damage, you take the difference of your Resolve minus theirs in Willpower points for each turn of contact, gaining those points (though excess Willpower is lost). If they no longer have Willpower, then they take it in Lethal damage, and their wounds worsen. After inflicting Lethal damage, some telltale traces often appears on you, such as a substance like blood seeping from your hands or eyes (which is actually Tass).<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> <i>You can't turn it off</i>. You probably won't be able to pursue medicine or comfort anyone injured again, knowing what you do to people. That is, unless you become addicted to your own life-draining and seek out people to victimize.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T19:20:33-07:00","id":1253190,"title":"","content":"<b>Supernal Focus (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 6+, Occult 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> The character has a highly defined sense of the connection to the Supernal World as it flows through the Fallen. This insight increases the maximum Yantra bonus from +5 to a bonus equal to the character's Gnosis rating.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The worst penalty possible due to various conflicting effects also becomes equal to Gnosis rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 09-12-2018, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T13:36:24-07:00","id":1258259,"title":"","content":"<b>The Soul in Motion</b> (\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural)<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Dexterity 3, Wits 3, Space 3<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Most beings are, on some level, static - stable enough that with the proper Imago, one can target them regardless of physical motion. The Mage breaks that rule. Her essence is motion. Her nature is flux. Any Sensory Range spell that would affect her rolls to hit as though it were Aimed (but with a +5 bonus) as the Imago slips off of her.<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>She cannot choose to lower this effect, and she cannot choose not to apply her Defense when targeted by spells (though if she's unconscious or otherwise immobile, she may not be able to do so).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-01T05:59:19-07:00","id":1258370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueWinds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1258259#post1258259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Soul in Motion</b> (\u2022\u2022\u2022, Supernatural)<br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Dexterity 3, Wits 3, Space 3<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Most beings are, on some level, static - stable enough that with the proper Imago, one can target them regardless of physical motion. The Mage breaks that rule. Her essence is motion. Her nature is flux. Any Sensory Range spell that would affect her rolls to hit as though it were Aimed (but with a +5 bonus) as the Imago slips off of her.<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>She cannot choose to lower this effect, and she cannot choose not to apply her Defense when targeted by spells (though if she's unconscious or otherwise immobile, she may not be able to do so).</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem: Supernatural Merits are restricted to humans (no major templates), while this mentions Mages and requires Space, which restricts it to Mages. It is literally impossible to take according to the rules. Dropping the Supernatural tag would be enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T14:31:21-07:00","id":1259124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1062942#post1062942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Edit:</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Four Rules </u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Style)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resolve 3, Gnosis 3</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You prefer releasing Paradox instead of containing. And you are good at it. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Drawback:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">???</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Anchor</u> (\u2022) - Substract dots in this merit from Paradox penalty to spells dice pool if released.<br /> <u>Anchor</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> v2 (\u2022) - Halve Paradox penalty to spells dice pool if released. Round down.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>xxxxxx</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022) - </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>xxxxxx </u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022) - </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hammer</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) - After ST rolled for Paradox you can spend Mana to cancel his successes with one-to-one ratio. You have do it in one turn and you are still limited by Gnosis and dots in this merit.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Is it okay for me to bring this back up? The concept really got me excited, but then it dropped from the conversation. Hopefully <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> will weigh the worthiness of my offering.<br /> <br /> I did like the offered drawback of more lasting Paradoxes from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12644_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12644\" data-vbnamecard=\"12644\">HerbertIsBestBert</a>. But maybe it should be a more personal drawback, like penalizing the check for Wisdom loss? Perhaps the style imposes a penalty of half your merit dots (round up) when releasing Paradox into your spells? If so it could drive the mage to using their inured spells to circumvent the drawback, consequently drawing down more Paradox. On the other hand, it could simply be viewed as a borderline Left-Handed practice, weaponizing releasing Paradox into the world. The Guardians of the Veil at the very least would take a dim view of those practicing this style. Even if using the style doesn't in itself justify hunting you down, increased scrutiny isn't very good for anyone in the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> As for the other two benefits, maybe something like these? Names are just my attempt at connecting the concept of the anchor to the hammer.<br /> <br /> <u>Fulcrum</u> (\u2022\u2022) - Whether due to meditating on the powers of your Path, studying the Paradoxes others have released upon the world, or just simple practice, you have become somewhat inured to the effects of your released Paradoxes. You gain a bonus equal to your dots in the style for resisting the effects of any Paradox Tilts you cause.<br /> <br /> (a) <u>Leverage</u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022) - You've improved your ability to gauge just how much paradox you incur in your spells. You can have the Storyteller re-roll the Paradox die pool <i>once</i> when you cast a spell. Use the result of the re-roll, even if more successes are rolled.<br /> <br /> (b) <u>Leverage</u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022) - You've worked hard at your spellcasting, and have become used to releasing Paradox into them. You gain a +1 bonus to your roll when you check for Wisdom loss whenever you cast a spell and release the Paradox.<br /> <br /> Notes: The style does feel like it's compensating for the harm you're incurring by releasing Paradox, capping with suppressing the Paradox with Supernal might. I hope <u>Fulcrum</u> is in keeping with this, as protection from your own Paradox over and above not suffering it yourself, while not generalizing the protection to <i>all</i> Paradox Tilts. <u>Leverage</u> depends on whether that protection extends to your Wisdom, or if you've internalized the fact that you are committing acts of hubris. If it does, I thought generalizing the protection might be a good idea, so those unable to transgress their Wisdom just from releasing Paradox don't feel left out. If it doesn't, letting the player weigh the odds on the Paradox roll might help with the capstone ability. If it feels too strong, perhaps limiting it to the character's Praxis? Or maybe something else, if this treads too far into Scelesti territory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5467-kagemcs","user":"KageMCS","date":".  Finally realized I didn't link the quote correctly. Or credit @HerbertIsBestBert. *facepalm* Hopefully I've fixed everything now. 10-07-2018, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5467-kagemcs","name":"KageMCS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-06T17:35:28-07:00","id":1259322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KageMCS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1259124#post1259124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe something else, if this treads too far into Scelesti territory?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it <i>surely</i> does that. Not that this is a bad thing, design-wise.<br /> <br /> I like the tone, here, which is non-judgmental. I'd consider making this a softer form of going Scelestus---Something that a character could rationalize or even like.<br /> <br /> Hmm: Perhaps add a Withstand rating vs. Paradox so the character is harder to affect directly with Paradox. It's not that Paradoxes are <i>reduced</i>, it's just that the merit means they aren't directly affecting the character. If you add the dice and Withstand at the same rate there will be more and bigger Paradoxes but the character will trend waltz through. They'll do more damage to everyone else and interfere with their own spells and such much less.<br /> <br /> Drawback, in that case, would seem to fit the theme. (Might just do a +1 to Paradox upgraded to +2 starting at 4, or something)<br /> <br /> Loss of a level of free Reach could be something to play with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","user":"thenate","date":". 10-06-2018, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-07T04:49:53-07:00","id":1259388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1259322#post1259322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the tone, here, which is non-judgmental. I'd consider making this a softer form of going Scelestus---Something that a character could rationalize or even like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can't take all the credit for that. Not originally my idea and all. Hopefully <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> doesn't mind us playing around with his toy too much.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I like that &quot;softer form of going Scelestus.&quot; I think it's what originally drew me. I'll adopt that as my platform.<br /> <br /> <b><i><u>SCELESTUS-LITE,</u></i><u> NOW WITH 0% BEFOULING, 100% &quot;F*CK CONSEQUENCES.&quot;</u></b><br /> <br /> I'm thinking the style falls in a very grey area, not interacting with the mechanics for Befouling your spells. Not directly anyways. I'd imagine there being some old masters of Four Rules who have never Befouled any of <i>their </i>spells and self-righteously hunting down those students they catch <i>straying</i>. A &quot;real&quot; Scelestus, meanwhile, might not view practitioners of this style as necessarily part of their ziggurat like the Rabashakim (cupbearers) are, instead viewing them as &quot;pilgrims&quot; passing by the ziggurat that might be called over to worship. (Had to go back and refresh my memory on the terminology. Reminded me why I like these guys and what <i>absolute pieces of work</i> they can be.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1259322#post1259322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm: Perhaps add a Withstand rating vs. Paradox so the character is harder to affect directly with Paradox. It's not that Paradoxes are <i>reduced</i>, it's just that the merit means they aren't directly affecting the character. If you add the dice and Withstand at the same rate there will be more and bigger Paradoxes but the character will trend waltz through. They'll do more damage to everyone else and interfere with their own spells and such much less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why you sly devil. I was just looking back and wondering how to protect the character from the Paradox Reach in their own spells. It's genius, and fits so well! I'd probably restrict that Withstand to your own Paradoxes though, just to keep the power from creeping up too much. If there's any organization to style practitioners, maybe they have friendly fire protection set into the style, but no more than that. So would adding the Withstand rating (equal to Potency, maybe?) be optional with an additional Paradox risk?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1259322#post1259322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Drawback, in that case, would seem to fit the theme. (Might just do a +1 to Paradox upgraded to +2 starting at 4, or something)<br /> <br /> Loss of a level of free Reach could be something to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like making more Paradox being the drawback. The whole style kind of revolves around taking the thought and care that's supposed to go into all spellcasting, and tossing it out the window. While making everyone else deal with the consequences. Wow, anyone who takes this style is kind of a dick. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I love it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And if we're going full Scelestus-lite here, I should probably withdraw my idea of the style interacting with Wisdom at all. Scelestus are all about nihilism, and nihilism is a complete disconnection from any and all moral structures. And I kind of dig baking the philosophical underpinnings into the mechanics. Plus we don't know what the Joining as an Integrity analog is going to look like, so I probably should've thought about that angle a little more. So I second <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar672_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"672\" data-vbnamecard=\"672\">thenate</a>, the main Drawback to the Four Rules (aside from being Scelesti-lite, and all THAT entails) is greater Paradox risk, reflected either as losing one free Reach, or always having a +1 to Paradox dice pools, whichever more elegantly fits with the main rules.<br /> <br /> Right now, Four Rules style looks like this with my and @thenate's ideas in brackets. Any version one benefits are <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a>'s original formulation. Added fluff in brackets because while I like fluff, I don't know what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1747_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1747\" data-vbnamecard=\"1747\">Moinen</a> will feel about it.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Four Rules </u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Style)</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Prerequisites:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Resolve 3, Gnosis 3</span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">You prefer releasing Paradox instead of containing. And you are good at it. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Drawback:</b> [You suffer greater Paradox risk. You lose one free Reach on all spells.]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Anchor</u> v1 (\u2022) - [The first step in this style is improving your chances at successfully casting your spells. You no longer suffer penalties to your spellcasting roll below a certain threshold.] Substract dots in this merit from Paradox penalty to spells dice pool if released.<br /> <u>Anchor</u> v2 (\u2022) - [The first step in this style is improving your chances at successfully casting your spells. You no longer suffer as great a penalty to your spellcasting roll.] Halve Paradox penalty to spells dice pool if released. Round down.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>[Fulcrum</u> (\u2022\u2022) - </span>Whether due to meditating on the powers of your Path, studying the Paradoxes others have released upon the world, or just simple practice, you have become somewhat inured to the effects of your released Paradoxes. You gain a bonus equal to your dots in the style for resisting the effects of any Paradox Tilts you cause.]<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>[Leverage</u> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(\u2022\u2022\u2022) - Further development of Fulcrum has extended your protection against Paradox Tilts to the Paradox in your own spells. You gain a Withstand rating equal to your spell's Potency effective against Paradox Reach.]</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hammer</u> v1 (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) - [You've achieved all Four Rules. You can now suppress Paradox Reach with Supernal power outright instead of managing chances.] After ST rolled for Paradox you can spend Mana to cancel his successes with one-to-one ratio. You have do it in one turn and you are still limited by Gnosis and dots in this merit.<br /> <u>[Hammer</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> v2 (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022) - You've achieved all Four Rules.</span> Through long practice, you can now better weigh the risk of Paradox in your spells. You can have the ST re-roll the Paradox dice pool <i>once</i> when you cast. Take the result of the re-roll, even if more successes are rolled.]<br /> <br /> I'm offering my Hammer version as an option if the Scelestus-lite feel is embraced, since suppressing Paradox with Mana doesn't feel like it fits with that theme. Plus it opens up the option of &quot;real&quot; Scelesti using it to <i>increase</i> Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5467-kagemcs","user":"KageMCS","date":". 10-08-2018, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5467-kagemcs","name":"KageMCS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T05:23:27-07:00","id":1259781,"title":"","content":"One of the dev blogs used to describe using Blood Sacrifices as a Sacrament to gain a Yantra Bonus equal to Mana gain, in lieu of Mana itself. It looks like that got cut from the book, but I thought it was pretty awesome, so I built a merit around the idea.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Blood Magic (Style, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022) </b></u><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Awakened, Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, Composure \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You are particularly adept at the twisted art of fueling your magic with living sacraments.<br /> <br /> <u>Blood-Stained Implements</u> (\u2022) -- You've learned how to preserve the lingering energies from a blood sacrifice, and by ritually coating a single magical tool in blood while performing a blood sacrifice, you may spend gained Mana to grant that tool an additional +1 Yantra bonus and expand it's semiotic associations appropriately for a single use per point of Mana spent.<br /> <br /> <u>Bound in Blood</u> (\u2022\u2022) -- Blood can serve as a powerful conduit for magical energies, and you've learned how to use it to leach the most harmful of them away. You treat blood sacrifice Sacraments as if they were a Dedicated Tool, and reduce Paradox accordingly. Alternatively, you may use Blood-Stained Implements to annoint a specific tool with blood and use it as a Dedicated Tool (replacing the +1 Yantra bonus), though this effect only persists for half as many uses as it otherwise would (round down, minimum 1).<br /> <br /> <u>Well of Sacrifice</u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022) -- When performing a Blood Sacrifice as a Sacrament, you may opt not to gain any Mana from the sacrifice, and instead replace the normal sacrament Yantra bonus with a bonus equal to the amount of Mana you would have gained. You may still utilize Blood-Stained Implements, reducing the sacrament Yantra bonus by one for each use, as though you were spending gained Mana on the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T12:19:18-07:00","id":1259850,"title":"","content":"I cannot recommend &quot;Doing First Tongue Translations&quot; thread enough. Among the First Tongue translations are some specifically Scelesti translations. So I made a request for a translation last thing before bed, and in the morning I found this waiting for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=1259554#post1259554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5467-kagemcs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5467\" data-vbnamecard=\"5467\">KageMCS</a><br /> <br /> \u200bId' propose either one (or both) of these:<br /> <br /> <b>A) Thirik-Harmathakhdul </b>(&quot;Extensive Traveller of the Fallen World&quot;)<br /> <br /> It mimics the distinction made by Werewolves and spirits between the title of <b>Gurihathakhdul </b>(&quot;one that has extensively travelled the Gurihal, the physical world of the Flesh&quot;) and this of <b>Hisithakhdul</b> (&quot;one that has extensively travelled the Shadow&quot;), but emphasizes on the world as it is Fallen (<b>thirik</b>: to fall, to collapse, to disintegrate; <b>Thirik-Harmatha</b>: the Fallen World).<br /> <br /> The reason for this emphasis in the case of an almost-but-not-quite-Scelesti is evident, though its exact implications are not that clear. Perhaps it cynically implies that Pilgrims are the only non-Scelesti mages that have seen enough of the Fallen World to understand how irremediably sundered from the Supernal it was, which makes them lucid enough to deal with the reality of the Fall rather than keep up vain and delusional pretenses of avoiding anything Abyssal. Unless it simply underlines that this reality Falls even lower everywhere a Pilgrim treads.<br /> <br /> <b>B)</b> <b>Yageken-Thun</b> (&quot;Travellers of the Void&quot;).<br /> <br /> (same construction as <b>Illusah-Thun</b>, &quot;the Travellers of Watery Trails&quot;, aka Riverkin)<br /> <br /> While &quot;Yageken&quot; (hole, void) is simply the First Tongue term for the Abyss,&quot;thun&quot; can either indicate the notion of travel (&quot;to move, to travel; to place elsewhere&quot;) or the idea of digging, rocking, or churning around. So Yageken-Thun could also be understood as &quot;Those who Displace the Void&quot; or &quot;Hole Diggers&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was all set to run with it, then I got a notification and found this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=1259689#post1259689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5467-kagemcs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5467\" data-vbnamecard=\"5467\">KageMCS</a><br /> <br /> Upon reflection\u2026<br /> <br /> The ranks in the Scelesti hierarchy are not in First Tongue, but in various, more tardive Semitic languages: Rabashakim derives from Rabashak, the name or term used to designate the envoy of an Assyrian king in the <i>Book of Nahum</i>, while Aswadim comes from the Arabian word aswad (\u201cblack\u201d). I think it\u2019d be more fitting (and cooler) to maintain that stylistical continuity. (Also, it might be handy to have a word that is less of a mouthful than Thirik-Harmathakhdul...)<br /> <br /> Hence, while the First Tongue terms I give you may still be accurate to describe the Pilgrims (or even any kind of Befouler) from the standpoint of an Uremehir speaker, I\u2019ve decided to submit to you a couple of terms in broken Akkadian. <hr /><br /> When speaking about Four Rules Pilgrims showing no interest in furthering their dealings with the Abyss, Scelesti refer to them as <b>Nakrim </b>or<b> Nakarim</b> (\u201cforeigners, strangers, enemies\u201d). The mere fact that an Awakened unbefouled could behold and make use of its dreadful wonders and <i>get away with it, </i>without paying the due toll in chaotic change and beautiful tragedy, is blasphemy without measure to them.<br /> <br /> Oppositedly, those who seem to embrace the tenets of the Scelesti and use their gifts to further their agenda receive the (slightly) less appellation of <b>Ub\u0101rim</b> (\u201cvisitors, guests; immigrants\u201d). While it also indicates a level of foreignness, it also denotates some measure of acceptance. For her eagerness and deviousness, the Pilgrim is tolerated: the Abyss is not yet her home, but it may be, one day.<br /> <br /> Lastly. those with full understanding of the Four Rules probably earn themselves the title of <b>Shanamzaqim </b>(from the Akkadian <i>\u0161a namzaqi</i>, <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;a doorkeeper, person in charge of keys&quot;</span></span>). Whether they gladly enter the building they spent so long to map and charter, finally merging with their Ziggurat, or simply swing open its gates without risking themselves in, Shanamzaqim are enablers to the Abyss, showering the world in its twisted blessings, and Scelesti respect that, however begrudgingly.<br /> <br /> Of course, the name of \u201cDoormen\u201d to qualify non-Scelesti unleashers and subduers of Abyssal Manifestations is not without reminding a certain Exarch of the Gate\u2026 (whistle gleefully in Parametric Language).</div> </div> </div> </div>And now Adrasalieth is my personal hero, for putting all that additional time and energy into my little request, and for dropping in a connection to the Gate. Please forward all likes to the original posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5467-kagemcs","user":"KageMCS","date":". 10-09-2018, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5467-kagemcs","name":"KageMCS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T04:39:19-07:00","id":1260105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1259781#post1259781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the dev blogs used to describe using Blood Sacrifices as a Sacrament to gain a Yantra Bonus equal to Mana gain, in lieu of Mana itself. It looks like that got cut from the book, but I thought it was pretty awesome, so I built a merit around the idea.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Blood Magic (Style, \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022) </b></u><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Awakened, Resolve \u2022\u2022\u2022, Composure \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Effect:</b> You are particularly adept at the twisted art of fueling your magic with living sacraments.<br /> <br /> <u>Blood-Stained Implements</u> (\u2022) -- You've learned how to preserve the lingering energies from a blood sacrifice, and by ritually coating a single magical tool in blood while performing a blood sacrifice, you may spend gained Mana to grant that tool an additional +1 Yantra bonus and expand it's semiotic associations appropriately for a single use per point of Mana spent.<br /> <br /> <u>Bound in Blood</u> (\u2022\u2022) -- Blood can serve as a powerful conduit for magical energies, and you've learned how to use it to leach the most harmful of them away. You treat blood sacrifice Sacraments as if they were a Dedicated Tool, and reduce Paradox accordingly. Alternatively, you may use Blood-Stained Implements to annoint a specific tool with blood and use it as a Dedicated Tool (replacing the +1 Yantra bonus), though this effect only persists for half as many uses as it otherwise would (round down, minimum 1).<br /> <br /> <u>Well of Sacrifice</u> (\u2022\u2022\u2022) -- When performing a Blood Sacrifice as a Sacrament, you may opt not to gain any Mana from the sacrifice, and instead replace the normal sacrament Yantra bonus with a bonus equal to the amount of Mana you would have gained. You may still utilize Blood-Stained Implements, reducing the sacrament Yantra bonus by one for each use, as though you were spending gained Mana on the effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Double post, but this is definitely worth promoting. A complete style (Inodiv sure is better put-together than I am), and one about living sacrifices. Isn't it just a bit twisted blood sacrifices are part of the innate template and not just an add-on? I like how you start out improving tools, leading up to using the sacrifice for a truly powerful Yantra itself. Oh, you can get a potent Yantra relatively easily, but what will it cost you? Really brings up images of Aztec and Mayan sacrificial rites in my mind, especially the first two dots. I realize &quot;magical tool&quot; could be anything, but &quot;knife&quot; immediately sprung to mind for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5467-kagemcs","name":"KageMCS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T08:11:58-07:00","id":1260137,"title":"","content":"I had this idea some time ago, but then completely forgot to post it:<br /> <br /> <b>Fortune Fracking (</b>\u2022\u2022\u2022<b>)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> All mages possess the ability to scour their physical forms for Mana, but some learn ways of converting more esoteric aspects of their Pattern into mystical power. With this Merit, a mage can voluntarily accept a Hex with a Potency up to their dots in Fate; in return, the mage gains a number of points of Mana equal to the Hex's Potency. The Storyteller designs the Hex, and, like resistant damage, it cannot be mitigated or dispelled by supernatural means. Use of this Merit counts toward the number of times per day a mage may scour their own Pattern.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T04:38:15-08:00","id":1269786,"title":"","content":"I came up with this Merit a while ago, but it might be of use for somebody!<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\">Magical Focus</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022 </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\">to </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\">)</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prerequisites</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Awakened, Arcanum at 3 or more.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Effect: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Once a Mage has studied an Arcanum deep enough to understand its basics principles, he can begin to specialize in a given field within the Arcanum. When you buy this merit, you must choose one purview within the Arcanum chosen. A few examples are: Death (shadows), Fate (boons), Matter (solids) and so on. When casting spells within the chosen purview, the mage can use this merit as persona Yantra with a bonus equal to the points in this merit minus 1. Also, once per game session, and before rolling the spellcasting roll, you can choose to have an exceptional success on 3 successes. You can purchase this merit only once for a given Arcanum, but you can purchase it for a number of different Arcana equal to your Gnosis.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24776,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","user":"Eleizel","date":".  Fixes the type of yantra and clarified how it works 11-30-2018, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","name":"Eleizel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T20:05:43-08:00","id":1271031,"title":"","content":"Perhaps just +2 for the 4 dot version?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T20:39:06-08:00","id":1271037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eleizel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1269786#post1269786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I came up with this Merit a while ago, but it might be of use for somebody!<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\">Magical Focus</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\">(</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022 </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\">to </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Metamorphous\">)</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Prerequisites</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Awakened, Arcanum at 3 or more.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Effect: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Once a Mage has studied an Arcanum deep enough to understand its basics principles, he can begin to specialize in a given field within the Arcanum. When you buy this merit, you must choose one purview within the Arcanum chosen. A few examples are: Death (shadows), Fate (boons), Matter (solids) and so on. When casting spells within the chosen purview, the casting roll gains a +1 to +3 bonus dice and counts as a Yantra. Also, once per game session, and before rolling the spellcasting roll, you can choose to have an exceptional success on 3 successes. You can purchase this merit only once for a given Arcanum, but you can purchase it for a number of different Arcana equal to your Gnosis.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Neat idea. I\u2019d clarify that the bonus is 1 per dot purchased after the initial 2 for purchase that grants +1. I\u2019d also specify what kind of Yantra the bonus is, or require that the player determine what kind of Yantra it will be. Like perhaps the one with Matter (Solids) decides that it will be an Environment Yantra tied to workshops and places where machinery are used/made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T03:02:19-08:00","id":1271948,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the reply! Actually, yes, it would give +1 with the 2 merit version, +2 with the 3 merit version, and +3 with the 4 one. As a yantra I think it should work like the shadow name works, as a persona yantra resonating with the focus and the studies you haver undergone for the chosen purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","name":"Eleizel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T03:05:11-08:00","id":1271949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1271031#post1271031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps just +2 for the 4 dot version?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have modified how the merit gives its bonus but it should work as this: +1 with the 2 merit version, +2 with the 3 merit version, and +3 with the 4 one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","name":"Eleizel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T09:04:00-08:00","id":1271989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eleizel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1271949#post1271949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have modified how the merit gives its bonus but it should work as this: +1 with the 2 merit version, +2 with the 3 merit version, and +3 with the 4 one</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw, but i still think that +3 bonuses are too powerful even for 4 dot merits, just personally. Even if it is limited in scope somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 11-30-2018, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T09:58:55-08:00","id":1272007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1271989#post1271989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I saw, but i still think that +3 bonuses are too powerful even for 4 dot merits, just personally. Even if it is limited in scope somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just depends on the power level you want in your game. For me it has been working fine, while on combat, the player almost always just add one yantra anyways, and while ritually casting, one more dice has never be too unbalanced, so if for you works better to limit the merit to +2, then just go for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","name":"Eleizel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T11:25:00-08:00","id":1272018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1271989#post1271989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I saw, but i still think that +3 bonuses are too powerful even for 4 dot merits, just personally. Even if it is limited in scope somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow Name costs less and is just as potent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T03:29:30-08:00","id":1272146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=1272018#post1272018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shadow Name costs less and is just as potent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing more to say XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24776-eleizel","name":"Eleizel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T14:34:27-07:00","id":1398873,"title":"","content":"It's thread necromancy, but I prefer that to a new thread.<br /> <br /> <b>Arcane Mind</b> (3,4, and 5 dot awakened merit)<br /> <i>Requires</i>: Gnosis 2, Wits 3, Prime 1, Occult 3<br /> <i>Benefits</i>: When a single item, action, or environmental Yantra has such alignment with the spell being cast that it could be used as a Yantra in multiple ways, the merit represents particular ease incorporating the symbolism. Significant symbolism is a form that, of itself, would provide a +1 or better Yantra bonus. <br /> <br /> The 3 dot version means that a Yantra that is being used in a single manner and which has at least 2 other forms of significant symbolism not otherwise incorporated into the casting can improve the Yantra bonus by +1. This can only be used on a single Yantra source at a time. The incorporation provides only an improvement to the primary Yantra incorporated and doesn't apply the benefits from the other forms, nor does it count against the total number of Yantra permitted.<br /> <br /> The 4 dot version means that incorporating at least 3 forms of the symbols at can provide a +2 bonus to the bonus of another use of the source. Otherwise, it works as the 3 dot version. This can still only be applied to a single Yantra source at a time.<br /> <br /> The 5 dot version allows multiple Yantras to be affected at a given time and otherwise works as the previous.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T22:34:45-07:00","id":1400008,"title":"","content":"<b>The Thorn's Scratch</b> (\u2022, Supernatural)<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Fate 1<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Naomi bears beneath her left eye a scratch - a scar left by a close encounter with the devil himself. She left behind a trace of blood and some of her ability to pass as normal, but, like a good witch, she took more than she gave. The scar can be used as a +2 yantra on any spell that Sleepers might witness. If used in this way, the spell is always obviously unnatural to anyone who succeeds on a roll of Wits + Occult - (Naomi's Manipulation), regardless of how subtle its effects might otherwise be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9510-bluewinds","name":"BlueWinds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"554"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T12:04:29-07:00","id":1478970,"title":"","content":"The following Merit is based on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/885111-homebrew-mage-merits?p=965813#post965813\"><b>Passionate Sorcery</b></a> by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a>.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Pathos Imago (\u2022 or \u2022\u2022)</b></u><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Mage<br /> <br /> You can draw upon emotion-based Conditions to fuel your magic. In other words, you gain a Yantra for spells which symbolically match the emotion. This Yantra gives +1 if the Condition is Persistent, +2 if it is non-Persistent. Furthermore, it increases by another +1 for each of the criteria below.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The spell will count as an Act of Hubris rolled with at least a -1 penalty after all modifiers are factored.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The spell automatically suffers a minimum of Paradox dice equal to your basic Over-Reaching (e.g. 1 Paradox die at Gnosis 1, 2 Paradox dice at Gnosis 3, and 3 Paradox dice at Gnosis 5). This cannot go lower through the usual methods of mitigation. This Paradox is not Abyssal in nature, and is closer to the type that affects Unsafely Relinquished spells over time.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The Condition would be Resolved by the spell if it is non-Persistent, or would give a Beat if it is Persistent.<br /> <br /> With the 1 dot version of the Merit, the emotion must be relatively specific. For example: anger towards the Seers Of The Throne, or fear of losing your Sleeper family. With the 2 dots version of the Merit, you can choose an entire category of emotion, such as joy or sorrow in general.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-16-2022, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T18:34:12-07:00","id":1484737,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Affirmation (\u25cf To \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b></u><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Dedicated Vow<br /> <br /> Your Dedicated Vow requires you to not only maintain a certain mundane type of conduct, but also requires you to proactively affirm it with your spells. For example: a pacifist Mage must use magic to prevent violence, while an honest Mage must use magic to reveal falsehoods. While upholding his Dedicated Vow, he gains a Yantra for the relevant spells equal to [Merit Rating]. He must dedicate one of his Gnosis-slots to benefit from this Yantra, as usual.<br /> <br /> However, if he casts a spell that goes against his code or principle of behavior, he not only loses the benefits of the Dedicated Vow, but it also counts as an Act of Hubris, which rolls a basic dice pool of [6 - Merit Rating]. Should this Act Of Hubris result in a Dramatic Failure, the resulting Persistent Hubris Condition does not have to be Resolved by losing another dot of Wisdom. Instead, the Mage can go through extreme complications or hardships to readopt the Dedicated Vow in a more committed manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-22-2022, 11:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}